{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision","id":1166925,"title":"Mage 5 and a new vision","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-12-12T00:03:35-08:00","id":1166925,"title":"Mage 5 and a new vision","content":"I recently checked out the alpha slice for V5, Vampire fifth edition, (the X20 books are now being regarded as an edition it seems) and it got me thinking about Mage 5.<br /> <br /> Now I believe the developers said they\u2019d be developing a fifth edition for werewolf and then Mage, though when that will be, who knows?<br /> <br /> The new direction for V5 is quite different from the previous editions, everything from how Vampires feed, to what it means to belong to the Camarilla has changed.<br /> <br /> This got me thinking, will Mage be reenvisioned as drastically?<br /> <br /> I for one hope so. I was never a fan of nWOD but I DO want to see a reenvisioned Mage the Ascension, one where the developers aren\u2019t afraid to make sweeping changes and try something new.<br /> <br /> I would even be open to significant changes to the Traditions and Conventions. <br /> <br /> I\u2019m curious how others feel. Is there any support for this or do people want Mage the Ascension to stick to the old material without really changing it?<br /> <br /> I feel it\u2019s acceptable to go in a new direction with the published material and don\u2019t want to see the new editions rehash the old material, BRING ON THE NEW!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","user":"Zennis","date":". 12-12-2017, 03:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T01:35:27-08:00","id":1166933,"title":"","content":"Well, WW clearly isn't afraid of drastic changes.<br /> <br /> That said, I don't want to see change for the sake of change (one of the reasons I've found the V5 material extremely disappointing is that most of the changes seem driven far more by wanting to look like they're radically altering the game, when they're just tossing in a few things on top of the same engine with what seems like very poor understanding of how it all slots together). And they seem to want the 5th edition stuff to be mechanically compatible-ish from their statements.<br /> <br /> I think the biggest problem for Mage, is that I can't really think of any direction to take it that isn't better served by other games. Ascension is firmly camped on the &quot;crazy philosophy wars over subjective reality&quot; thing. If you try to pull it into other directions, you're in competition with Awakening, Unknown Armies, the Dresden Files RPG, Kult, Witchcraft, CoC, etc. There's a lot of modern day magic user games out there, and most of them do other takes on the concept really well.<br /> <br /> There's plenty of sacred cows the game can afford to slaughter, but in the end, what's the point of a Mage 5th edition that doesn't actually play like Mage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T03:44:45-08:00","id":1166943,"title":"","content":"I think if there would be another edition of M:tA, then one of the main goals should be to develop the Nephandi into a more complex faction of True Mages.<br /> For example, currently there isn't enough material in the M:tA books to enable and make it possible for a player to have a Nephandus True Mage as their character; a storyteller or a player has to add a lot additional information, interpretation and background in order to do so.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zennis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision#post1166925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would even be open to significant changes to the Traditions and Conventions.</div> </div> </div> </div>What kind of changes to the Traditions and the Technocracy's Conventions would you suggest in a new edition of M:tA ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T05:05:59-08:00","id":1166954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zennis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision#post1166925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m curious how others feel. Is there any support for this or do people want Mage the Ascension to stick to the old material without really changing it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I like Ascension as it is, even a bit more during the Revised metaplot. I think it has the best iteration of the Storyteller engine and maybe the second-best setting after Wraith, so while I think there is room for improvements I don't think it's a game that needs them much.<br /> <br /> That said, there is nothing preventing me to keep playing Revised if I want, so what's the point of a the-more-the-same new edition? While I still rather play Ascension I kinda liked the new take on the Awakening game line, it gave us something different and that's really the most important thing IMHO. So I'd say: please hit me with something original, I can always stick to the old if I don't like it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T06:32:04-08:00","id":1166973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1166933#post1166933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, WW clearly isn't afraid of drastic changes.<br /> <br /> That said, I don't want to see change for the sake of change (one of the reasons I've found the V5 material extremely disappointing is that most of the changes seem driven far more by wanting to look like they're radically altering the game, when they're just tossing in a few things on top of the same engine with what seems like very poor understanding of how it all slots together). And they seem to want the 5th edition stuff to be mechanically compatible-ish from their statements.<br /> <br /> I think the biggest problem for Mage, is that I can't really think of any direction to take it that isn't better served by other games. Ascension is firmly camped on the &quot;crazy philosophy wars over subjective reality&quot; thing. If you try to pull it into other directions, you're in competition with Awakening, Unknown Armies, the Dresden Files RPG, Kult, Witchcraft, CoC, etc. There's a lot of modern day magic user games out there, and most of them do other takes on the concept really well.<br /> <br /> There's plenty of sacred cows the game can afford to slaughter, but in the end, what's the point of a Mage 5th edition that doesn't actually play like Mage?</div> </div> </div> </div>That.<br /> <br /> To me V5 feels a lot like shoving the Masquerade Metaplot into a Requiem style setting-I don't like that. M5 should play like Mage.<br /> <br /> I could be OK with A LOT of changes in the mechanics as long as they don't depart from the core concepts of the game-Rote rules would be nice, I wouldn't mind mechanical compatibility between the lines, Spheres and Paradox have been changed before-as long as they do respect the core concepts of the game I'm fine with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T10:24:09-08:00","id":1167038,"title":"","content":"I'd be looking for something which makes Mage less daunting to new players. The general mechanics aren't too difficult, but there need to be less byzantine systems than in M20 How Do You Do That? and more information for the player who isn't going for heavy lore immersion into how to make a character.<br /> <br /> While there is a conversion guide, you really need both Awakening and Ascension to use the conversion guide. I've found other system conversion guides that flow well without having both books.<br /> <br /> Perhaps rather than looking for a Mage 5th edition, White Wolf could carefully craft Storyteller's Vault guidelines for Mage. Mage, being a game about the nature of reality and how to transform it, is well-suited to many different opinions as long as they are well-written and delivered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T11:41:49-08:00","id":1167062,"title":"","content":"HDYDT might have been less byzantine if it didn't completely contradict both the M20 core and itself at various points. Lack of consistency has always been one of the strongest and weakest parts of Mage. Strong in that it pushes people to not worry too much about a one true way, weak in that it tends to get people completely lost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T14:25:32-08:00","id":1167133,"title":"","content":"I think that the biggest change they need is to make the ascention war a real war. The last couple editions, especially revised, it was more the technocrasy just tormenting a bunch of tradition mages who had no real chance of winning. If you want to make a war setting interesting both sides of the conflict have to have a reasonable chance of victory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/706-rickayelm","name":"rickayelm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T16:04:22-08:00","id":1167175,"title":"","content":"See, I think the reverse is happening. As time goes on it seems the Traditions are depicted as closer to evenly matched with the Technocracy. They are not on an even footing, but they are a far cry from the shattered resistance on the run from the overwhelming power of the Man that they were in years gone by. For that matter the Technocracy is far from the overwhelming power of the Man.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T22:14:14-08:00","id":1167224,"title":"","content":"The council was slaughtered like defenseless children, and the traditions are now led by a group of movie producers hiding in the Alps. Not exactly my idea of being anywhere near evenly matched.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/706-rickayelm","name":"rickayelm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T23:22:03-08:00","id":1167231,"title":"","content":"Would anyone be open to the Traditions being reworked? That is, change up exactly what groups comprise the Traditions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-13T00:12:21-08:00","id":1167234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1167231#post1167231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would anyone be open to the Traditions being reworked? That is, change up exactly what groups comprise the Traditions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you think it would be new True Mage groups, or would it be Crafts, or a group(s) made up of former members of a Technocracy Convention?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-13T00:15:41-08:00","id":1167236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1167231#post1167231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would anyone be open to the Traditions being reworked? That is, change up exactly what groups comprise the Traditions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I totally am. In fact I would like the Traditions ot be reworked, I\u2019m open to a council of Nine with 9 new players or a council of 17 with some only and some new.<br /> <br /> I actually would like to see a reworking fo the Traditions and a whole new take on the mystical societies of the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-13T09:42:25-08:00","id":1167337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1167175#post1167175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> See, I think the reverse is happening. As time goes on it seems the Traditions are depicted as closer to evenly matched with the Technocracy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say that the Traditions are depicted in M:tA as being evenly matched with the Technocracy, in regards to the capabilities of their True Mages and, for example, the intricacy of the groups and organizations that exist within Traditions. I think this is especially clear once a person takes into account that the Technocracy's Conventions are simillar to the individual Traditions, in regards to the fact that the True Mages that are part of the individual Conventions don't have the same amount of cooperation between them that the True Mages within the same Tradition or the same Convention do have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-13T13:10:56-08:00","id":1167397,"title":"","content":"As an aside... If the concepts of Mage in 5th (if it comes about) are even close to those in previous edition you still should not, ever, have a Nephandus as a player character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-13T23:19:18-08:00","id":1167530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moirdryd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1167397#post1167397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As an aside... If the concepts of Mage in 5th (if it comes about) are even close to those in previous edition you still should not, ever, have a Nephandus as a player character.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why do you think so?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T03:53:51-08:00","id":1167562,"title":"","content":"They're eminently villains, a scourge upon everything that matters. Their very existence marks an aggression against the world, and any new material on them should keep that in mind.<br /> Can there be more on them? Sure. Look up the hermetic and jewish kabbalahs on Qliphoth and you'll understand why the nephandic magick get that tag.<br /> <br /> Writing them as something more playable? I doubt that will be done, don't think currently it should be done, and I doubt someone like phil will ever take part in that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":32,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","user":"Synapse","date":". 12-14-2017, 06:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T04:31:05-08:00","id":1167569,"title":"","content":"Yep. They are walking wilful evil wrapped in flesh and twisting True Magick. They are at the very extent of wickedness incarnate and are there by choice bound by an act of their on will. They are NPC Villains (not just antagonists but villains) of the highest and most terrifying and terrible order, there is no Tragedy to their existence, no noble cause in their being, no responsibility in action, no one and nothing matters to them except them and the path they have chosen. The world is Their World and they love nothing but breaking, corrupting and hurting and they can be clever about it but that's always what the go for, whatever they touch they spoil, rot and ruin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T04:55:43-08:00","id":1167573,"title":"","content":"Oh...no... That's not what I was thinking at all. <br /> <br /> White Wolf started out from the position of &quot;Let's play MONSTERS&quot; and then made the monsters kinda-sorta good guys with a &quot;but these over there.. They're the REAL baaaaaaaaaad ones.&quot; Then went and made each and every one of them into playable options. I mean, what?, there are rules for characters from the Sabbat, Baali, Black Spiral Dancers, Fomor, Specters, etc. Nephandi doesn't seem like much of a stretch at all. What about a Nephandi can really be more qualitatively evil than the Sabbat? I mean, c'mon, Giles de Rais (such a model for Nephandi that his name is the source of their term for a really, most sincerely bad, awful, powerful Nephandus) and his little parties are pretty much the equivalent of a Sabbat Blood Feast or a family of necromancer cannibals dinner party or a Shadow Court version of a Wild Hunt or even just well-produced Harrowing. Not dancing with the dark side doesn't seem like a terribly good reason to keep a group out of the mix for PCs. <br /> <br /> I was thinking the fact that it's going to have significant negative effects on player agency. The reason most people won't want to play Nephandi is the same reason they probably wouldn't want to play Marauders. The Cauls make a Nephandus different from a normal human, like Quiet renders one of the Mad unable to interact with Consensual Reality on the same basic level as other characters (including NPCs). Now they are hard-wired for Decension. How many people want to play a character where it's not just entirely legitimate, but integral to the underlying concept for the ST to say not just &quot;Your character won't do that&quot; but &quot;Your character can't even conceive of doing that&quot;? Even if a character is being played so that they go with the evil flow, there are going to be a lot of times that being a post-Caul un-human is going to be as limiting as playing a Marauder within the limitations of their Quiet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T06:45:30-08:00","id":1167593,"title":"","content":"Nephandi get about as much love as fomori in their write up.<br /> <br /> They appear here and there (normalizing for rarity), and have each their own book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T06:49:27-08:00","id":1167594,"title":"","content":"Can you tell me sincerely that the Mage is a monster in the same way a Vampire is? Or a Werewolf? Or how they compare to each other?<br /> <br /> Your usage of &quot;MONSTERS!&quot; barely gets past Vampire, where the whole ordeal stems from &quot;you are an immortal monster playing your cloak and dagger societal games&quot; ; where indeed the Sabbath is not that different from the rest of them. A black spiral is an outright perversion of everything the other b\u00eate stand for. A nephandus is closer to that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T07:22:41-08:00","id":1167603,"title":"","content":"Notably, BSD aren't any more &quot;playable&quot; that Nephandi. And Vampire have their &quot;unplayable&quot; bad guys which even the Sabbat loaths...though not sure why speaking with the Devil it's worse than what the Sabbat does.<br /> <br /> And about mages being &quot;monsters&quot;. Well, they certainly aren't build like that. You can do it, but unlike Vampire, Demon, Wraith or even Werewolf, in Mage there aren't any mechanics that would push you to act like the classic <i>evil wizard/wicked witch</i>.<br /> <br /> There's no Beast, Rage nor &quot;decaying Moral&quot; in Mage. There's no &quot;Shadow&quot; speaking in your ear and tempting you with evil powerz. If you're bad it's because you want to be like that, and there's no reward. Worse, Paradox may frustrate or punish a lot of attempts of classic &quot;evil witch scaring mortals&quot; interaction. In my opinion, Mages suck at being <i>&quot;Monseters!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Mages, from a &quot;WoD of terror where you play the monsters&quot; perspective, are more like the Illuminaty conspiracy thing that knows stuff and controls humanity. They can be scary, and &quot;prey on humans&quot; in a fashion, but they're hardly &quot;monsters&quot; in the <i>classic sense</i> (they can be &quot;monsters&quot; in the same senses humans can-but that's not the point of playing a supernatural creature, isn't it?).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T09:02:02-08:00","id":1167666,"title":"","content":"If you don't think mages are monsters, you haven't really seriously thought over what it would be like to be a Sleeper in a world where mages are real and where one of them is interested in you. Or, perhaps worse, one in which a mage is doing something nearby and you are innocent bystander. . <br /> <br /> They don't need a decaying moral statistic or something to struggle against. They are pretty much amoral assholes with limitless power from the get go with pretty much just fancy botches to keep them in check. Even if they do have some &quot;code&quot; it's very likely that it doesn't really take your well-being as you see it into account. They are very much monsters in the Classic sense, if your &quot;classic sense&quot; includes tragedy or psychology and not the Hollywood Movie Monster pantheon. Mages are reality terrorists. <br /> <br /> You CAN play a Fomor (and yes, I have seen it done and done as well or better than most Werewolf characters) Or a Specter. Or a Baali working for the Black Hand. Or a Dunsirn Revenant. Or an Infernalist. There isn't a single line White Wolf ever drew saying &quot;These guys are just TOO eeeeeeeevil for players&quot; that they didn't later cross. Except, maybe for Nephandi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T11:15:22-08:00","id":1167715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1167666#post1167666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You CAN play a Fomor (and yes, I have seen it done and done as well or better than most Werewolf characters)</div> </div> </div> </div>I've seen it done, and it was actually really, REALLY cool.<br /> <br /> Very, very tragic. Heroic as well, but the ending was definitely tragic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T11:40:56-08:00","id":1167724,"title":"","content":"I'm personally dreading what kind of changes M5 would take to be considered &quot;drastic&quot;, considering the changes that Revised and M20 made were drastic enough in my book.<br /> <br /> But then again, I'm not supporting NuWW outside of the Storyteller's Vault so maybe I should not complain. I've still got my Mage 2e corebook to keep me company. If others like Revised, M20, or the hypothetical M5, then that's cool with me. You do you and I'll do me.<br /> <br /> That being said, on a more productive note, I would LOVE to see Mage: The Ascension added to the Storyteller's Vault so we can see fan-made material for previous editions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T11:42:09-08:00","id":1167726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1167715#post1167715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've seen it done, and it was actually really, REALLY cool.<br /> <br /> Very, very tragic. Heroic as well, but the ending was definitely tragic.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you ever feel like playing a fomor in the Chronicles Of Darkness. Try Deviant the themes are very Alike","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T12:11:10-08:00","id":1167734,"title":"","content":"The core mechanics in V5, while not perfect and final and there are things I'd like to see change, but seem to be a good start, so I'm okay with those as the new WoD core.<br /> <br /> Regarding magick, I'd like to see something easier to grasp to new players, maybe more defined rote rules, but it's too early to speak about anything, without any grasp of their ideas.<br /> <br /> As for the setting: I'm getting to came into terms with the known V5 changes, but I still think some of it could be too much. I got the impression, from some interviews with them on the web, that they're playing with the idea that, while the Union isn't good, the Traditions aren't either. Basically, Orwellian Big brother and soulless machine vs. Religious Fanatics. Maybe they'd run with the extrapolation of M20's New millenium, where the Disparates are the &quot;good guys&quot;, just as V5 seems to be anarch-centric somewhat. I dunno. Honestly, I'd be glad about a lot of the New Millenium's stuff being the baseline. I'm somewhat expecting a vibe that every organization is a dick and oppressive in some way and you are the little guy. I'd be... okay with that, I guess as long as the organizations aren't 2bit villains either, but playable and having their good points.<br /> <br /> What I don't want to see is radical rewriting of the setting. changes are OK, shifting allegiances, policies, new groups even are OK, but it'd better be recognizable as Mage in the end.<br /> <br /> I think they said on the Darker Days show that they think Brucatto did a very good job with M20, so there's that. Ultimately, I think it's just too far away in the future and it's just some ideas floatng around in their heads, not any clear concept. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T13:13:09-08:00","id":1167756,"title":"","content":"Meh, I did not like Brucato's changes to M20, especially the addition of the Disparates.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-15T05:03:37-08:00","id":1167873,"title":"","content":"The disparates are among the least impactful changes M20 had. It's just a continuation of the ascension war petering out: the struggle between the factions is dwindling down, a bunch of factions that never really worked with any of them are gaining a bit of significance and they kinda sorta acknowledged each other as a way to keep the traditions and conventions off their necks.<br /> <br /> Are you sure you're not unhappy with the fact that the ascension war's losing momentum, instead?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-15T05:28:43-08:00","id":1167876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1167873#post1167873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you sure you're not unhappy with the fact that the ascension war's losing momentum, instead?</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, no. I never liked the ascension war except as a setting element that informs some of the choices of character. I prefer Revised when the Ascension War was done and nobody cared anymore about the consensus.<br /> <br /> I dislike the the disparates because on one hand the way are presented as the &quot;is the traditions guys, just not problematic&quot; which defeats the purpose of the traditions vs technocracy in that both arent exactly good. And that they lack sense, groups that ideologically shouldnt work together (the templars for example) do so because somehow the bigger concern of the Nephandi overrun they petty beefs. When the Nephandi threat isnt as public and general to warrant that kind of response.<br /> <br /> It doesnt feel earned, It just feel like yet another of Brucatto ego\u00b4s stroke for him to say &quot;Look guys, i fix the mistakes of the past now you can play the tradition which are politically correct&quot; with his usual lack of understanding of the issue at hand. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1167603#post1167603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Notably, BSD aren't any more &quot;playable&quot; that Nephandi. And Vampire have their &quot;unplayable&quot; bad guys which even the Sabbat loaths...though not sure why speaking with the Devil it's worse than what the Sabbat does.</div> </div> </div> </div>That true tough the BSD are technically playable with book of the wyrm 20. You make a normal garou and then buy some of the Wyrm gift and flaws and there you go. <br /> <br /> Same with the Nephandi, you make a mage.....and mechanically that it. Unless I am forgetting some special rule their change (inverted avatar) dont have any change to the day-to-day mechanics of them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1167603#post1167603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And about mages being &quot;monsters&quot;. Well, they certainly aren't build like that. You can do it, but unlike Vampire, Demon, Wraith or even Werewolf, in Mage there aren't any mechanics that would push you to act like the classic <i>evil wizard/wicked witch</i>.<br /> <br /> There's no Beast, Rage nor &quot;decaying Moral&quot; in Mage. There's no &quot;Shadow&quot; speaking in your ear and tempting you with evil powerz. If you're bad it's because you want to be like that, and there's no reward. Worse, Paradox may frustrate or punish a lot of attempts of classic &quot;evil witch scaring mortals&quot; interaction. In my opinion, Mages suck at being <i>&quot;Monseters!&quot;</i></div> </div> </div> </div>I think like in Werewolf that play in the game favor. A problem with I have with Chrod is the use of objective moralities of any kind. OwoD (werewolf and Mage) didnt had those, you dont get easy answer of whats right and wrong you just gotta figure that out on your own. <br /> <br /> Is making a cult of underage teens to make drugs bad when you pick them from the streets, give them a home and food and sense of belonging and forge them into a cult so making drugs with magic is easier? On one hand, yes is abominable. On the other.....is better than them being on the street.<br /> <br /> <br /> Personally what I hope for M5 that i definitely wont get is: Mage revised, with better rules and a restraining order that Brucatto wont put its hands on any mage product ever again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-15T09:25:39-08:00","id":1167938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1167876#post1167876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That true tough the BSD are technically playable with book of the wyrm 20. You make a normal garou and then buy some of the Wyrm gift and flaws and there you go.<br /> <br /> Same with the Nephandi, you make a mage.....and mechanically that it. Unless I am forgetting some special rule their change (inverted avatar) dont have any change to the day-to-day mechanics of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that was my whole point. <br /> <br /> BSD haven't any more &quot;agency&quot; than Nephandi, once you walk the black spiral you're pretty much harcoded to be evil. It doesn't matter if you were a relatively nice guy before, Entering the labyrinth and embracing it's nature it's pretty much the same as entering a Caul and accepting the transformation. If you believe Nephandi aren't playable because what Ajax said before (agency and stuff), then you don't beleive BSD are playable because they have a relationship with evil that's analogous as that of Nephandi<br /> <br /> Phill says you shouldn't play with Nephandi, but if you believe that this is an argument, then you're accepting that Kiasyd are &quot;unplayable&quot; too (something I see no one accepting).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-15T10:04:29-08:00","id":1167946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is making a cult of underage teens to make drugs bad when you pick them from the streets, give them a home and food and sense of belonging and forge them into a cult so making drugs with magic is easier? On one hand, yes is abominable. On the other.....is better than them being on the street. </div> </div> </div>Humans can do that...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you don't think mages are monsters, you haven't really seriously thought over what it would be like to be a Sleeper in a world where mages are real and where one of them is interested in you. Or, perhaps worse, one in which a mage is doing something nearby and you are innocent bystander. .</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I have. Perhaps you are missing my point, there's more about being a monster that being evil. In fact, I would say that being a monster, in the classic sense, does not imply being evil.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They don't need a decaying moral statistic or something to struggle against. They are pretty much amoral assholes with limitless power from the get go with pretty much just fancy botches to keep them in check. Even if they do have some &quot;code&quot; it's very likely that it doesn't really take your well-being as you see it into account. </div> </div> </div>Missing my point.<br /> <br /> You're generalizing, I can name mages and mage organizations of the top of my head that aren't &quot;amoral assholes&quot;: Like the whole faction of Extatics that dedicates to save victims of child abuse and punish pedophiles. In general, you may be correct, albeit it's debatable, but you're missing my point.<br /> <br /> My WHOLE POINT was that <i>you're evil only if you want to be evil, which it's a completely free choice that the game in no way advertises.</i> I never stated that there aren't whole organizations of Eeeeeeevil mages that love being evil. I merely stated that since you don't have any mechanic that rewards or pushes you towards being evil, then Mage it's not more a game of &quot;playing the monster&quot; than D&amp;D. In that sense of being a Monster...<br /> <br /> Now, let's explore other senses.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They are very much monsters in the Classic sense, if your &quot;classic sense&quot; includes tragedy or psychology and not the Hollywood Movie Monster pantheon. Mages are reality terrorists. </div> </div> </div>Hollywood Movie Monster pantheon. Let's see, what's that pantheon made off ?. Vampires (Vampire), werewolves (Werewolf), the frankenstain monster (In CoD, they finally came). Wicked witches and noble wizards are part of Hollywood (see Oz) but the good ones are hardly characterized as monsters...<br /> <br /> Now. WoD it's , literaly, made of &quot;the Hollywood Movie Monster pantheon&quot;. It takes a novel approach to the genre where, say, werewolves may be justified in what they do because they fight cosmic horrors, but I don't see why you would think that anyone should include in their classic sense anything but that pantheon. We're speaking about WoD after all, the games where you play with said pantheon, not with greek tragedy (where monsters weren't even that bad compared with humans) nor psychology.<br /> <br /> However, if you want to go to other works about monsters, fine, let's do it. Let's go to Greek mytology. Try to make a &quot;Circe&quot; like character, she was a &quot;wizard&quot; type after all: You need a Master of Life and Paradox may not like it. As a play stile, it sucks, Mage rewards being subtle. Thus, Mage it's bad at playing greek monsters too.<br /> <br /> There's no &quot;reality terrorists&quot; in any classic work about mosnters, as far as I know, but fell free to illuminate me and demonstrate why Mage it's the game that's supposed to be played like that. The closest thing I can think off it's the Illuminatus trilogy, which isn't that old, ad isn't what I would call &quot;monster literature&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You CAN play a Fomor (and yes, I have seen it done and done as well or better than most Werewolf characters) Or a Specter. Or a Baali working for the Black Hand. Or a Dunsirn Revenant. Or an Infernalist. There isn't a single line White Wolf ever drew saying &quot;These guys are just TOO eeeeeeeevil for players&quot; that they didn't later cross. Except, maybe for Nephandi. </div> </div> </div>And you missed my point by a mile, as I stated above.<br /> <br /> But, since you have your doubts about Nephandi being playable because just because they do have said line, then perhaps you believe that Kiasid are unplayable too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 12-15-2017, 01:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-15T10:13:47-08:00","id":1167950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1167876#post1167876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Personally what I hope for M5 that i definitely wont get is: Mage revised, with better rules and a restraining order that Brucatto wont put its hands on any mage product ever again.</div> </div> </div> </div>Same here, only for me it's Mage 2e instead of Revised. Nothing personal against Satyros Brucato, but I don't like the sweeping changes that Brucato made to M20. It was just too much for me.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-15T14:11:07-08:00","id":1168020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1167950#post1167950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Same here, only for me it's Mage 2e instead of Revised. Nothing personal against Satyros Brucato, but I don't like the sweeping changes that Brucato made to M20. It was just too much for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, as someone who's played every edition of Mage at some point or another, M20 doesn't feel all that sweeping. To me, M20 feels like a Mage 2.5+e. Its got some of Revised's DNA in the bashing/lethal damage divide, but the Magick is very much in line with 2e (particularly in terms of Paradox and how it builds and is discharged), with the main change to magick being using a holistic Focus (paradigm/practice/props) and pulling at Mythic Threads instead of the individual specialized foci that 2e/Revised did.<br /> <br /> I don't mind either of those changes though because what I've found is that they helped a lot of my newer players grok Mage a lot better than the older rules did and replacing &quot;using a sphere's specialized focus&quot; with &quot;use a mythic thread&quot; as one of the tools for reducing magick difficulties made the players more apt to try and think about what sort of means and ends their tradition/craft/convention is associated with (ex. chanting in latin while scrawling symbols on the ground in chalk in order to summon a spirit or throw a fireball for a Hermetic) far more than just the list of props and using the right one at the right time for that -1 difficulty bump ever did.<br /> <br /> The softer 2e style paradox (relative to Revised) also made them much more apt to actually use vulgar magic in line with their paradigm because it was now worth the risk (i.e. 1 point that doesn't blow up immediately unless you're at 5+ banked paradox and might bleed off as paradox flaws instead vs. taking 4+ that blows up immediately for bashing damage if you're trying to throw a fireball in public).<br /> <br /> Other than that, just about all the updates were fluff updates the book went out of its way to say you could ignore. Including the disparates and conventions is just par for the course with the other 20th Anniversary editions because they're meant to be extremely comprehensive on that stuff (V20 including all the bloodlines/specialty disciplines and W20 including all the other changing breeds for example).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-15T14:27:01-08:00","id":1168023,"title":"","content":"<br /> I wouldn't like M5 to portray the Traditions as fanatic zealots. Guide to the Traditions has the model that I want the Traditions to follow, with mixed Traditions and a greater acceptance for science.<br /> <br /> I loathe, as I have stated many times, the M20 idea of painting the Trads as facist and creating a group of &quot;new traditions&quot; that are more politically correct than the previous one. Sadly, that does seem to be the actual course of action, and would fit with the &quot;edginess&quot; of the new books.<br /> <br /> I really like the way M20 has upgraded the rules, I may have a qualm here and there, but, frankly, I played with &quot;reality zones&quot; before they were a thing, I like the Mythic Thread stuff, I like Focus mechanics, and the Paradox and dice rules are pretty much like the 2ed rules I use. There's little I don't like from the way M20 does magick, altrough they explain it very poorly.<br /> <br /> And while I wouldn't mind playable Nephandi (aren't they a thing already?), I wouldn't want to paint them as &quot;misunderstood&quot;. I like my Fallen to be corrupt, thank you.<br /> <br /> But, like so many people said, I have my books, I have my group-I can play however I want. Thus I don't care a whole lot. <hr /><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">My WHOLE POINT was that <i>you're evil only if you want to be evil, which it's a completely free choice that the game in no way advertises.</i> I never stated that there aren't whole organizations of Eeeeeeevil mages that love being evil. I merely stated that since you don't have any mechanic that rewards or pushes you towards being evil, then Mage it's not more a game of &quot;playing the monster&quot; than D&amp;D.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps a clarification it's in order. Let me exemplify:<br /> <br /> I have an Etherite that's a paranormal detective. He's an adventurer and has always defied danger and avoided death by a hair split, but he never killed anyone. He loathes violence too, albeit he's not above giving information to hunters or the like if a creature relly needs to be put down. I modeled the character with some inspiration from The Doctor, in that he wouldn't use a gun. Also, he won't kill a monster just because the creature preys on humans. Vampires have to feed too and it's in their nature.<br /> Now, his presence can be very enigmatic, sometimes even scary to the onlooker when he does uncanny stuff (trough I try to resort to Coincidence), but he wouldn't be called, nor call himself, a &quot;monster&quot;.<br /> <br /> I have a Brujah that was a humanist philosopher. Very high on Humanity, he values not only human life but human rights<i>. Or he used to.</i>You see, with my best intentions I couldn't avoid Frenzi forever. He fellt atracted to human blood, and he wasn't always able to contain this <i>unhuman </i>desires. He was horrified by his dependance on fresh blood, and loathed being a vampire.He's not a bad guy (even now, with Humanity 4, I don't think about him as a <i>bad guy</i>, he's just more willing than before to &quot;take hard choices&quot;, and don't care about feeding on humans if this helps against the Beast)<i>, but he believes to be a monster, and for all the right reasons</i>-he did not choose the Curse but wasn't about to suicide either.<br /> <br /> Vampire has a lot of mechanics thar reward being a monster, like Humans giving more blood, Diablere being the path to power. Vampire <i>seems </i>to discourage this with the menace of the Beast, but this same mechanic forces you to do bad stuff even if you don't want to. Playing the drama of not wanting to be bad while you're, undoubtedly, a monster it's not only encouraged by every part of the fluff, but very cleverly aided by the rules.<br /> Mage has nothing of that. Mages are very free, this does include a (mostly unrewarded, sometimes punished) potential to play the monster, but really, the game isn't about that. Nothing in the game pushes you towards that gaming experience, at least not more than D&amp;D pushes you towards evil alignments.<br /> <br /> But well, nuf said about that. Let's just say that the way I play Mage wouldn't be compatible with making it &quot;a game about playing the monsters&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 12-15-2017, 05:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-15T15:47:18-08:00","id":1168033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1168023#post1168023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't like M5 to portray the Traditions as fanatic zealots. Guide to the Traditions has the model that I want the Traditions to follow, with mixed Traditions and a greater acceptance for science.</div> </div> </div> </div>I liked that portrayal of the traditions too, although I'm not against showing their darker sides either. I'm just saying that, when the WW guys were asked about Mage, they tended to be saying a few ideas about how the world seems to heading to the direction of global surveilance and cop state vs. religious and ideological fanaticism and I agree Mage should speak bout that. Now, the how and how much is an entirely different question, I don't want to see the Trads as solely zealots and terrorists either. A portion of it, sure, but not the whole.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I loathe, as I have stated many times, the M20 idea of painting the Trads as facist and creating a group of &quot;new traditions&quot; that are more politically correct than the previous one. Sadly, that does seem to be the actual course of action, and would fit with the &quot;edginess&quot; of the new books. </div> </div> </div>I'm not pointing at you, but I notice people on the internet seems to regard everything authoritarian, or even militaristic as fascism. Not a big deal, but mildly annoying, IMO.<br /> <br /> I'm not totally hating the Disparates, I just find it very stretching that those groups would form any kind of widespread alliance with each other.<br /> <br /> Agree about the rules.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-15T16:07:52-08:00","id":1168042,"title":"","content":"Most of my issues with M20 are the changes to the setting and the fluff, namely the inclusion of the Disparates. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-15T18:37:57-08:00","id":1168081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1167938#post1167938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that was my whole point.<br /> <br /> BSD haven't any more &quot;agency&quot; than Nephandi, once you walk the black spiral you're pretty much harcoded to be evil. It doesn't matter if you were a relatively nice guy before, Entering the labyrinth and embracing it's nature it's pretty much the same as entering a Caul and accepting the transformation. If you believe Nephandi aren't playable because what Ajax said before (agency and stuff), then you don't beleive BSD are playable because they have a relationship with evil that's analogous as that of Nephandi<br /> <br /> Phill says you shouldn't play with Nephandi, but if you believe that this is an argument, then you're accepting that Kiasyd are &quot;unplayable&quot; too (something I see no one accepting).</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, i agree nothing mechanically stops you from playing a nephandi or a BSD. Both are perfectly playable from RAW. That said i would never run or play in such game but that my taste.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1167946#post1167946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I merely stated that since you don't have any mechanic that rewards or pushes you towards being evil, then Mage it's not more a game of &quot;playing the monster&quot; than D&amp;D. In that sense of being a Monster...</div> </div> </div> </div>There is kind of one though. Revised resonance, the basic idea being that the more you use magic in a certain way the better you become at that type of magic at the cost others.<br /> <br /> Example in the last game i play at, one of the character got 5 entropic resonance (pain) so all his magic caused searing pain. He used to have rote to heal people but he couldnt use it anymore without his resonance tainting his magic and healing while causing searing maddening pain. What that good or bad? Neither, when he wanted to attack his resonance was useful to him but when he wanted to heal people it wasnt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-15T18:44:21-08:00","id":1168083,"title":"","content":"I have long learned to filter out political opinions shoehorned into my entertainment - as it very much is with m20 (though so surprisingly little for how Phil lives his life I almost forget he penned it).<br /> <br /> Maybe I just ignore it effortlessly and thus I cam get on to enjoying the entirety of the game without worry of haranging.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-15T20:37:22-08:00","id":1168109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1168042#post1168042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most of my issues with M20 are the changes to the setting and the fluff, namely the inclusion of the Disparates.</div> </div> </div> </div>But the Disparates have been around since the Book of Crafts was published in 1996. If something's been around for more than two decades its not a new change. All they did was put them in the core along with the Technocracy... just like the V20 book included every last minor bloodline and their custom disciplines and the W20 book included the werecats, rats, ravens, dinosaurs, sharks, et cetera. Because the 20th Anniversary editions were intended to be as all inclusive of the elements of their particular setting as possible.<br /> <br /> The &quot;Alliance&quot; bit is stuff that, as they point out with all the fluff (and particularly with the Future Fates sections) can be used or IGNORED as you desire. The idea was to make a one-stop inclusive reference for EVERYONE, not a &quot;You must play this way and only this way&quot; product which was essentially the bane of the Revised Edition (i.e. using stuff like the Avatar Storm, wiping out the masters to force and all their &quot;you're doing it wrong if you're not doing street level dying magic game&quot; comments rife in that edition to push the OneTrueWayism of Revised's authors).<br /> <br /> Instead M20 is all about options. It gives options for using it during Revised era events (by including the rules you'd need to do that if you wanted), presuming Revised era happened but is over now (the default) and even as if Revised NEVER HAPPENED and things kept plugging along as they were in 2e (Doisetep and Horizon never fell, Porthos and all the Old Masters are still around, etc.). The storyteller and players get to pick the sort of story they want to tell.<br /> <br /> It sounds like your biggest gripe with M20 is that it offered people options instead of straight-jacketing everyone to your preferred style. I much prefer M20's &quot;play the game you want to play&quot; approach... it feels more true to the core concept of Mage... that reality is subjective and can be shaped to your own personal desires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-16T08:38:45-08:00","id":1168194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1168109#post1168109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The &quot;Alliance&quot; bit is stuff that, as they point out with all the fluff (and particularly with the Future Fates sections) can be used or IGNORED as you desire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Regardless, it's there, not even as a future fates box, but in the core writeups of the groups, so I think it's fair for someone not liking it, for whatever reason. I don't have serious gripes with it, I just felt it pretty stretching as an assumption that those groups would band together (they are very contrary to each other, usually lacking any central authority, etc.) and yes, it has some contemporary American political undertones, which isn't necessarily bad, I don't have problems with including political questions into the game, but it felt a little bit forced. I mean, in a way that the group's existence isn't really very-well justified within the setting internally, but by the author's political view. Mind, I'm not saying it is wholly bad, since as I read it, it's more like &quot;we don't cross each other and provide some measure of basic help and camaraderie, if necessary&quot;, than any kind of organized cooperation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The idea was to make a one-stop inclusive reference for EVERYONE, not a &quot;You must play this way and only this way&quot; product which was essentially the bane of the Revised Edition (i.e. using stuff like the Avatar Storm, wiping out the masters to force and all their &quot;you're doing it wrong if you're not doing street level dying magic game&quot; comments rife in that edition to push the OneTrueWayism of Revised's authors). </div> </div> </div>Yeah... I started with the revised-era books (and with Vampire), back in the day and yes, it was painstakingly clear that the writers had their strong opinions about how the games &quot;should&quot; be played and even contemptous derision toward certain things. I just learned later on that it was mostly targeted toward their own fans and earlier editions. Nowadays, I prefer too if a book provides resources for all kinds of play, be it somewhat epic-toned, with lots of action and supernatural elements or street level, with lots of self-reflection and daily problems, or the mix of the two and the writers don't taking up blatant stances and condemning the others. I don't need the writers to tell me that I'm wrong if my mages in a game about magic and mages dare to throw around some fancy spells, from time-to-time, or that my vampires should burn in the morning if they ever dare to pick up a trenchoat.<br /> <br /> Truly, it was yet again case of things going too far and then the retaliation being just as too extreme. On the other hand, Revised might be my favorite edition of WoD visually.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Instead M20 is all about options. It gives options for using it during Revised era events (by including the rules you'd need to do that if you wanted), presuming Revised era happened but is over now (the default) and even as if Revised NEVER HAPPENED and things kept plugging along as they were in 2e (Doisetep and Horizon never fell, Porthos and all the Old Masters are still around, etc.). The storyteller and players get to pick the sort of story they want to tell. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I liked that too. Honestly, that is my favorite version (ie. that the revised era happened, but things are recuperating since), because you know what? The Revised era is a good story (IMO) and interesting as an era. I just don't want it to be the baseline forever, because it's also quite depressing on the long run. I think the writers recognized that and even softened up on things, even during Revised's run.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 12-16-2017, 11:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-16T12:12:42-08:00","id":1168231,"title":"","content":"I don't like the disparate alliance much ether to be honest<br /> <br /> The whole group seems like a bad fit for its member crafts <br /> <br /> I find the idea little hard to swallow for the simple reason that these groups don't strike me as even being capable of working together in a meaningful way, particularly the Taftani and the Batini and the Sisters of Hypolita and the Knights Templars. <br /> <br /> If these groups can work together then they can work with some of traditions<br /> <br /> this idea that the disparate alliance has banded together but won't work with the Trads because apparently they've been infiltrated by the nephandi strikes me as a little unbelievable.<br /> <br /> Now I don't mind the disparate alliance at all aside from the above issue. I like most of the groups and even more, I like the idea of them coming to the traditions and saying &quot;we can't be pushed around and we won't be forced to assimilate into one of the nine of you, so either get a bigger number and let us in as equals or lie in the bed you make for yourself without us!&quot;<br /> <br /> I also find the name to be a poor choice, I don't think they would call themselves that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-16T22:00:56-08:00","id":1168309,"title":"","content":"Wait... How does M20 portray the Traditions as fascist or as just a bunch of religious fanatics? Maybe I missed something (the book is pretty freaking big) but I don't remember the Trads getting trashed that hard by Phil. In fact, I think he kind went of his way to make them straight up good guys.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-17T00:31:04-08:00","id":1168321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1167876#post1167876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It doesnt feel earned, It just feel like yet another of Brucatto ego\u00b4s stroke for him to say &quot;Look guys, i fix the mistakes of the past now you can play the tradition which are politically correct&quot; with his usual lack of understanding of the issue at hand.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">\u200bYou were given a week suspension last summer for making personal attacks against Phil Brucato, this time it's a month. If you come back and the behavior doesn't change for the better then the next suspension will be permanent.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-17T00:36:13-08:00","id":1168325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weirdboyz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1168309#post1168309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait... How does M20 portray the Traditions as fascist or as just a bunch of religious fanatics? Maybe I missed something (the book is pretty freaking big) but I don't remember the Trads getting trashed that hard by Phil. In fact, I think he kind went of his way to make them straight up good guys.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the worry is that is what WW will be doing with M5, not what happened with M20.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-17T04:35:33-08:00","id":1168347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Personally, no. I never liked the ascension war except as a setting element that informs some of the choices of character. I prefer Revised when the Ascension War was done and nobody cared anymore about the consensus. </div> </div> </div>I like Revised more exactly because the Masters were cut out from the Earth: this gives the newbie players more weight and responsibilities on the events taking place, removing at the same time the hassle of having elders born in the 15th century shaping your life from Doissetep. Even if I never like the new Discorporation rule, even that helps keeping the plot on Earth rather than removing the mages from the world altogether.<br /> <br /> Of course, having rules and options to choose which campaign to run is better than a straight line, but it wasn't honestly that hard to cut those extras off Revised if you didn't like them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I dislike the the disparates because on one hand the way are presented as the &quot;is the traditions guys, just not problematic&quot;. </div> </div> </div>Are they? I think they're just poorly written.<br /> The Sisters of Hippolita are almost a joke: the same philosophy of the Verbena and the same structure of the Black Furies (but without their background): it seems they were only created to mock Feminism. The Templars do the same thing of the Choristers, just with an extra spin on fanaticism... and by the way, how the hell can they get along with the Hippolitai, or Voodoo practictioner?<br /> The Taftani seem to have lost their whole point of existence with the passage into M20: they were a group of mages iron-bent on fighting the Consensus through public Vulgar magick displays and they despised the Traditions for submitting to the Technocracy through the use of coincidental magic; now they're using coincidental effects, technomagic and still despising the Traditions enough to not join them? What the hell?<br /> The Hollow Ones murdered hundreds of Tradition mages with their betrayal of Concordia, so much for not causing problems; I'm surprised they're still around, they probably won't for much longer if the Euthanatoi manage to get back in shape. Also, isn't Goth Magick a bit out of fashion now? And the Orphans, yeah, they shouldn't really mingle with the Disparates any more than with theTraditions.<br /> <br /> My overall idea about the Disparate is that either they're poor copies of the Traditions or mage societies that were downgraded to make them fit with the others. Really, I may use a couple of them but as an alliance they're horrible.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Let's go to Greek mytology. Try to make a &quot;Circe&quot; like character, she was a &quot;wizard&quot; type after all: You need a Master of Life and Paradox may not like it. As a play stile, it sucks, Mage rewards being subtle. Thus, Mage it's bad at playing greek monsters too. </div> </div> </div>Every fantasy wizard topos needs to change a bit to fit Mage, though, because the Paradox is neither in the Odyssey (and it wouldn't be, morphing people was coincidental back then) nor any other fantasy book. Also it's not like you can't mass morph people, you just need to spend some extra effort and make it vulgar... but it's not like a diff 8 Life effect is going to be an impossible task.<br /> <br /> Btw, Circe wasn't really a &quot;monster&quot;... her story is a bit more than turning people in pigs. =P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-17T08:28:30-08:00","id":1168379,"title":"","content":"For M5, I think how WW will handle the Anarchs and the Camarilla in the setting books planned to be released with the core book would be somewhat of an indicator, since the Traditions are somewhat a mingle of the two.<br /> <br /> My best bet is that the traditions will get more fractured. The extremist groups will get more ground and they will be causing more problems internally and with the Union. At the same time I think the same will happen with the Union, as it strains under the conflict between the Orwellian (maybe Nephandi-influenced) part and the &quot;we genuinely want a better place for the masses to live in&quot; part. So I think the more moderate factions in both will close some distance between them and the extremist factions will be worse than ever and thus the strict Traditions vs. Technocracy dichotomy will loosen up.<br /> <br /> At least I think that would be the logical choice, based on their snippets. It's possible they'll go full nuts and the Union will be like in 'ye olde days and the Traditions will be bigots and religious fanatics and the Disparates will be the good guys, but I don't think that's extremely likely, based on their positive stance on M20.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1168347#post1168347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like Revised more exactly because the Masters were cut out from the Earth: this gives the newbie players more weight and responsibilities on the events taking place, removing at the same time the hassle of having elders born in the 15th century shaping your life from Doissetep. Even if I never like the new Discorporation rule, even that helps keeping the plot on Earth rather than removing the mages from the world altogether.<br /> <br /> Of course, having rules and options to choose which campaign to run is better than a straight line, but it wasn't honestly that hard to cut those extras off Revised if you didn't like them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agree with the last part. The problem is not that someone might like that style better. The same things were said about Requiem, back in the day (no elders, PCs in the spotlight, keeping it local, etc.) and a lot of people liked that better. That's good and all. The problem is, there was a big part of the game that a lot of other people liked too and it got cut off. On hindsight, i still think it was good for the setting and the story, it's an interesting era and shook up and loosened up the stalemate of the Ascension War, which is good, but I'm happy that it's over and I hope M5 will take that route. I liked the new Convention books' story, i liked the New Millennium, it'd be a bummer to go back to the Revised worldview and double back on it. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Are they? I think they're just poorly written.<br /> The Sisters of Hippolita are almost a joke: the same philosophy of the Verbena and the same structure of the Black Furies (but without their background): it seems they were only created to mock Feminism. The Templars do the same thing of the Choristers, just with an extra spin on fanaticism... and by the way, how the hell can they get along with the Hippolitai, or Voodoo practictioner?<br /> The Taftani seem to have lost their whole point of existence with the passage into M20: they were a group of mages iron-bent on fighting the Consensus through public Vulgar magick displays and they despised the Traditions for submitting to the Technocracy through the use of coincidental magic; now they're using coincidental effects, technomagic and still despising the Traditions enough to not join them? What the hell? </div> </div> </div>That's somewhat fair (although I don't think the groups are that bad). I have the same problem, that some of the groups just seem incompatible with each other for any real cooperation. Also, they lack central leadership, which could enforce that and even, the justification for the Alliance 8the Nephandy threat) is more or less just a rumor. I'm not saying the Disparates should go, but I do think they need more story tothem about the hows and whys.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Hollow Ones murdered hundreds of Tradition mages with their betrayal of Concordia, so much for not causing problems; </div> </div> </div>I still want to read the exact details of that. Even if they did, it wsn't really a &quot;they&quot;, as far as I'm aware, just one splinter member.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm surprised they're still around, they probably won't for much longer if the Euthanatoi manage to get back in shape. </div> </div> </div>Don't think so, there are much more Hollowers out there than Euthanatoi, at least in the West, I think. Also, they aren't exactly an easy group to pin down and they even got allies. Also, it was more than a decade and a half ago, I'm not counting on any pogroms to happen now. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, isn't Goth Magick a bit out of fashion now? </div> </div> </div>Heh, no. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Goth didn't die out and even having a comeback in the past few years. Besides, Hollowers aren't even &quot;just goth kids&quot;, they started waaaay back before goth was a thing, like centuries back. Do your research! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And the Orphans, yeah, they shouldn't really mingle with the Disparates any more than with theTraditions. </div> </div> </div>I don't see Orphans as a group. I think they are just individuals, who tend to have a preference for hanging out with the least jackass, least hard-assed minor groups, instead of the big organizations. Thus, the Disparates, although.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-18T11:27:32-08:00","id":1168574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1168379#post1168379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agree with the last part. The problem is not that someone might like that style better. The same things were said about Requiem, back in the day (no elders, PCs in the spotlight, keeping it local, etc.) and a lot of people liked that better. That's good and all. The problem is, there was a big part of the game that a lot of other people liked too and it got cut off.</div> </div> </div> </div>M20 offered a lot of options because it was an enormous, expensive manual and had the room to cover several alternative settings, but not every game can afford that. I still expect it to push the setting forward in time and evolve the setting, but maybe the optional timelines will be covered in other books.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's somewhat fair (although I don't think the groups are that bad). I have the same problem, that some of the groups just seem incompatible with each other for any real cooperation. Also, they lack central leadership, which could enforce that and even, the justification for the Alliance 8the Nephandy threat) is more or less just a rumor. I'm not saying the Disparates should go, but I do think they need more story tothem about the hows and whys. </div> </div> </div>My second big &quot;what&quot; about the Disparates (the first being how dull some of their groups are) is exactly that: how can they work together? &quot;Traditions are heterogeneous too&quot; yes, with less fanaticism though. Honestly I think they should be considered independents, just like those clans in the Masquerade: can be ally, can be rival, can be the center of a chronicle but what they can't be is a third power pole.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I still want to read the exact details of that. Even if they did, it wsn't really a &quot;they&quot;, as far as I'm aware, just one splinter member. </div> </div> </div>They joined a revolt that broke out in Concordia and later used their access privileges to let the Technocracy in, basically because they were tired of being excluded from the Council. I read in another thread that you can find a synopsis of that era in &quot;Tales of Magick: Dark Adventures&quot;, maybe it's easier to find than the novels.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Don't think so, there are much more Hollowers out there than Euthanatoi, at least in the West, I think. Also, they aren't exactly an easy group to pin down and they even got allies. Also, it was more than a decade and a half ago, I'm not counting on any pogroms to happen now. </div> </div> </div>They have allies only if you assume the Disparate work as the traditions, but as previously noted the lack of a central government and their different worldviews may suggest they're mostly on their own and join forces only to hunt down the Nephandi. And don't write off the Euthanatoi... they're the killers of the Awakened world and did the same thing for a lot of Tradition marks in the ages; they probably don't have the resources to carry out a proper Pogrom like the Technocracy but a faction war isn't that out of question IMHO.<br /> I'd really like to see this kind of active set-up in the 5th edition tbf.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-18T12:25:51-08:00","id":1168595,"title":"","content":"The biggest thing the Disparates provide, to my mind, is the chance to do an early days of the Traditions story, but in the modern world. A bunch of groups that don't really understand each other trying to work together for mutual protection and for a simple seeming ideal that no two of them understand in the same way. They even have some common origin elements. They are the initial idea, stripped of hundreds of years of historical baggage, and freed up with the potential to become anything. At the same time, they have none of the Tradition's experience at dealing with massive cultural differences and cross paradigm communication. They're primed and ready to either make the same mistakes or brand new ones depending on what the players do.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-18T16:07:23-08:00","id":1168660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1168574#post1168574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My second big &quot;what&quot; about the Disparates (the first being how dull some of their groups are) is exactly that: how can they work together? &quot;Traditions are heterogeneous too&quot; yes, with less fanaticism though. Honestly I think they should be considered independents, just like those clans in the Masquerade: can be ally, can be rival, can be the center of a chronicle but what they can't be is a third power pole.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Anarchs are just like that. As I said, I don't see the Disparates as a &quot;real&quot;, formal alliance.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They joined a revolt that broke out in Concordia and later used their access privileges to let the Technocracy in, basically because they were tired of being excluded from the Council. I read in another thread that you can find a synopsis of that era in &quot;Tales of Magick: Dark Adventures&quot;, maybe it's easier to find than the novels. </div> </div> </div>I know that, but if I remember correctly, it was one person, but I might be wrong, I have to check.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They have allies only if you assume the Disparate work as the traditions, but as previously noted the lack of a central government and their different worldviews may suggest they're mostly on their own and join forces only to hunt down the Nephandi. And don't write off the Euthanatoi... they're the killers of the Awakened world and did the same thing for a lot of Tradition marks in the ages; they probably don't have the resources to carry out a proper Pogrom like the Technocracy but a faction war isn't that out of question IMHO.<br /> I'd really like to see this kind of active set-up in the 5th edition tbf. </div> </div> </div>I'm not writing of the Euthanatoi, I just think that yes, they could (and would) kill quite a few Hollowers, from the more flashy ones and especially bordering on being barabbi, but on the whole, the Hollowers are just more numerous and good at staying underground and tending their own business. Also, contrary to popular beliefs, since they are essentially on their own, they aren't exactly pushovers either. They don't have the luxury.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I'm totally not anticipating any world-wide pogrom from the Traditions against the Hollowers, it's just too much of a hassle, without the serious chance of success. Also, again, a whole generation grown up since then. &quot;Concordia? what Concordia? Killing the Hollowers? You mean Phil??? We go to partying tohgether. Besides even my master says the archmages and the old council were serious dicks and treated others like shit, i'm not surprised someone at some point have had enough...&quot;<br /> <br /> So, that's for a wide pogrom. Oh, don't get me wrong, it's pretty sure, though that there will be some fanatic/bitter/desperate Traditionalists, who lost someone during those tumultuous times and hell-bent to taking it out on the poor Hollow kids locally and it's a great story seed, IMO. But no, I won't hold my breath for this thing going worldwide, after, almost exactly 20 years.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-18T23:24:10-08:00","id":1168727,"title":"","content":"I wish to remind everyone that one of the main reasons presented for why the Hollow Ones would join the Disparates is BECAUSE of the actions of the Horizon Warrior. They would be getting allies and potential cover. Picking off lone Hollow Ones might seem like a good idea to hardline Traditionalists, but it might seem less so when those Hollow Ones are starting to organize, and now have made friends with a dozen other Crafts. If the Hollow Ones join the Disparate Alliance, anyone who would make war on them must suddenly make war on the Bata'a, the Templars, the Wu Lung, and those slippery Ahl-i-Batin.<br /> <br /> That's a fight even the Tradition mages would not relish. Especially since the Traditions already have their on-and-off conflicts with the Technocracy, who most would agree are the greater threat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-18T23:36:27-08:00","id":1168729,"title":"","content":"Honestly v5 comes off very much as an attempt to put the Genie back in teh bottle and go back to an imagined 1e feel, before the Sabbat was anything but boogeymen, where Anarch vs Cam was the biggest game in town. With that in mind I don't think Nephandus are going to be on the table, or the Traditions are going to become a Magical Camarilla, I expect we will get a solid regression on the Technocracy's part to unplayable boogie man who keeps everything in check. I mean they've even played up some of the issues with the &quot;New inquisition&quot; being driven by Technocracy being tired of Vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T05:12:42-08:00","id":1168772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1168595#post1168595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The biggest thing the Disparates provide, to my mind, is the chance to do an early days of the Traditions story, but in the modern world. A bunch of groups that don't really understand each other trying to work together for mutual protection and for a simple seeming ideal that no two of them understand in the same way. They even have some common origin elements. They are the initial idea, stripped of hundreds of years of historical baggage, and freed up with the potential to become anything. At the same time, they have none of the Tradition's experience at dealing with massive cultural differences and cross paradigm communication. They're primed and ready to either make the same mistakes or brand new ones depending on what the players do.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd love to agree with you. Well.... I do. That's the intent.<br /> <br /> But the execution is abyssmal and, ultimately, unworkable. Even taking into account the &quot;This is how these groups CAN work together. See, here is the &quot;justice system&quot; that irons all that out&quot; from the Book of Secrets, it's just not going to fly based on how groups of people can, do and have worked together, or not, historically and prehistorically speaking. Some of these groups WILL NOT play well with each other (e.g. the Hippolytans, the Templars, the Kopa Loei, the Taftani) without compromising themselves to the point that the thing which defines them (for the most part, that self-same NOT-compromising to the eccumenicism of the Traditions) will be lost. The various groups that came to Convocation had a pressing reason to TRY to work together. More than one, even. The hegemony of the Order of Reason via the Age of Exploration/Colonialism was coming (and pretty much all the groups had diviners and prognosticators of some point. That's a common &quot;thing&quot; in the vast majority of cultures' mysticism). Plus there was an ongoing change in the way the fundamental base code of &quot;How Magic Works&quot; that had reached a tipping point. The only real reasons for the Disparates to come together that seems to be presented in M20 is &quot;The Nephandi are EVERYWHERE and we're the only uncompromised&quot; with a tinge, a very slight tinge and only with a few of the groups, that together is stronger/safer/easier to hide that apart. Plus some centuries old grousing about how things went down with the rise of the Traditions and the Order (and the ideological combination of the two... thanks Batini) and a dash of willful ignorance.<br /> <br /> They may be the Traditions without all the baggage, but, boy, do they carry a TON of baggage of their own and it's certainly not really dealt with at all. Whatever various &quot;original sins&quot; and past bad acts the Tradtitions are lugging around, the Disparates are just as encumbered with modern issues. Specifically rabid ethnocentrism and it's cousin, ideological purity.<br /> <br /> Maybe if the whole thing was a web manipulated by the Batini who were approaching each group as a sort of anti-Nephandi and using them as operational fronts, I might be able to buy it better. &quot;No the Templars and the Sisters don't have to work together. The Templars are great at X. The Sisters are great at Y. That's how we use them and that's how they should be used.&quot; Perhaps with some &quot;greater plan&quot; than just rooting out Nephandi (which is, admittedly, effectively one of the Seven Pillars of Batini-dom) they might be trying to manipulate them enough that they could work together some day. (I was toying with the idea that some of the groups (Ngoma?) might be &quot;in on it&quot; but, after thinking about it, I doubt it. The Subtle Ones would be being less than subtle. working against their strengths and throwing a show into the works.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1062,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","user":"Ajax","date":". 12-21-2017, 11:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T08:27:20-08:00","id":1168803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1168772#post1168772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd love to agree with you. Well.... I do. That's the intent.<br /> <br /> But the execution is abyssmal and, ultimately, unworkable. Even taking into account the &quot;This is how these groups CAN work together. See, here is the &quot;justice system&quot; that irons all that out&quot; from the Book of Secrets, it's just not going to fly based on how groups of people can, do and have worked together, or not, historically and prehistorically speaking. Some of these groups WILL NOT play well with each other (e.g. the Hippolytans, the Templars, the Kopa Loei, the Taftani) without compromising themselves to the point that the thing which defines them ( for the most part, that self-same NOT-compromising to the eccumenicism of the Traditions) will be lost. The various groups that came to Convocation had a pressing reason to TRY to work together. More than on, even. The hegemony of the Order of Reason via the Age of Exploration/Colonialism was coming (and pretty much all the groups had diviners and prognosticators of some point. That's a common &quot;thing&quot; in the vast majority of cultures' mysticism). Plus there was an ongoing change in the way the fundamental base code of &quot;How Magic Works&quot; had reached a tipping point. The only real reason that seems to be presented in M20 is &quot;The Nephandi are EVERYWHERE and we're the only uncompromised.&quot; Plus some centuries old grousing about how things went down with the rise of the Traditions and the Order (and the ideological combination of the two... thanks Batini) and a dash of willful ignorance.<br /> <br /> They may be the Traditions without all the baggage, but, boy, do they carry a TON of baggage of their own and it's certainly not really dealt with at all. Whatever various &quot;original sins&quot; and past bad acts the Tradtitions are lugging around, the Disparates are just as encumbered with modern issues. Specifically rabid ethnocentrism and it's cousin, ideological purity.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Is that a bug or a feature, though? Most of that can easily be worked as problems for the Disparates in game, and much of it was something the Traditions also had to deal with. The Disparates are a mad idea, at least as mad as the Traditions were and probably moreso since they are trying to deliberately avoid the same outcome.<br /> <br /> Were I to do anything with them, I'd set them on such a precarious balance that they <i>will</i> fall apart unless the players are actively trying to keep them together.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T09:15:04-08:00","id":1168815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1168729#post1168729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly v5 comes off very much as an attempt to put the Genie back in teh bottle and go back to an imagined 1e feel, before the Sabbat was anything but boogeymen, where Anarch vs Cam was the biggest game in town. With that in mind I don't think Nephandus are going to be on the table, or the Traditions are going to become a Magical Camarilla, I expect we will get a solid regression on the Technocracy's part to unplayable boogie man who keeps everything in check. I mean they've even played up some of the issues with the &quot;New inquisition&quot; being driven by Technocracy being tired of Vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>One sign to the contrary of that is that Technocracy characters were playable at the Berlin LARP, which has a significant place in the future metaplot. So, I don't think they'll go that far back to early Mage.<br /> <br /> As for Vampire, yes, I have too the definite impression that <i>at first</i> they want to go for an 1e feel. Although they said they <i>will</i> bring out the Sabbat, just not at the beginning, because they want to focus on the Cam vs. Anarchs thing at first. The Sabbat won't be an undefined boogeyman, they'll just show up later on.<br /> <br /> As I wrote earlier, I think it's most likely that extremist groups within both large organization will become more on the front and causing trouble, while the more moderate ones wanting to build bridges.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T09:20:57-08:00","id":1168817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1168803#post1168803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is that a bug or a feature, though? Most of that can easily be worked as problems for the Disparates in game, and much of it was something the Traditions also had to deal with. The Disparates are a mad idea, at least as mad as the Traditions were and probably moreso since they are trying to deliberately avoid the same outcome.<br /> <br /> Were I to do anything with them, I'd set them on such a precarious balance that they <i>will</i> fall apart unless the players are actively trying to keep them together.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd add one thing: the European Union. Yes, it has its own issues, but, given the thousands of years of history of Europe, all the grudges, the national, ideological and religious differences and hating, would you have thought they'd cobble together anything like that? It took two world wars within a century to do so but they did, in the end, because nobody wanted a third.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T10:32:52-08:00","id":1168844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1168803#post1168803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is that a bug or a feature, though? Most of that can easily be worked as problems for the Disparates in game, and much of it was something the Traditions also had to deal with. The Disparates are a mad idea, at least as mad as the Traditions were and probably moreso since they are trying to deliberately avoid the same outcome.<br /> <br /> Were I to do anything with them, I'd set them on such a precarious balance that they <i>will</i> fall apart unless the players are actively trying to keep them together.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would put it down as &quot;doomed to failure&quot; as is, but that doesn't mean it might not be fun to play out the doom. And there are definitely different kinds of ways that it can fail, one of which is that it can succeed, but end up like the Traditions, with the rough edges (by which I mean &quot;core concepts&quot;) are smoothed down (by which I mean &quot;drowned like unwanted kittens&quot;). Or it could fail forwards and shuck the groups that really CAN'T play well with the others and go forward with a subset that can function under some facsimile of the internal organization methodology described. <br /> <br /> But it seems more likely to end tragically and horribly and probably end up being a Nephandi plot to gather up the last groups that opposed them for easier disposal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T10:50:01-08:00","id":1168848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1168817#post1168817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd add one thing: the European Union. Yes, it has its own issues, but, given the thousands of years of history of Europe, all the grudges, the national, ideological and religious differences and hating, would you have thought they'd cobble together anything like that? It took two world wars within a century to do so but they did, in the end, because nobody wanted a third.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's existed for, what? 24 years? I'm not going to use it as the trumpet of rationality over the weight of irrational history until we see if it can last longer than a quarter of a century. And it's definitely got it's cracks and it's baggage. Brexit matters. As does the intransigence of considering Turkey for membership but being entirely cool using them militarily. The EU has been around about as long as it took for the Nine Traditions to become a nearly permanent 8.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T11:20:30-08:00","id":1168862,"title":"","content":"More like half a century, if you count its predeccesors. It means generations grown up without any wars within its borders and that we don't have to bother with paperwork within when traveling, etc. And I didn't say that that the EU will last, that's still up for grabs, neither did I suggested the same with the disparates. The thing is, it's an example that people could be willing to sit down and compromise, even after centuries upon centuries of grudges and after twice burning down the continent. It's possible. Yes, those old grievances and new interests might cause it to crumble, but seeing them making a starting attempt is not <i>that</i> stretching.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 12-19-2017, 02:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T11:49:53-08:00","id":1168868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1168862#post1168862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More like half a century, if you count its predeccesors. It means generations grown up without any wars within its borders and that we don't have to bother with paperwork within when traveling, etc. And I didn't say that that the EU will last, that's still up for grabs, neither did I suggested the same with the disparates. The thing is, it's an example that people could be willing to sit down and compromise, even after centuries upon centuries of grudges and after twice burning down the continent. It's possible. Yes, those old grievances and new interests might cause it to crumble, but seeing them making a starting attempt is not <i>that</i> stretching.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to agree that the EU is a good template both in what can be accomplished and also in the political problems that start getting in the way (whether those problems are real or imagined). Old grudges of course, and when the alliance goes back (sometimes necessarily) on its original promises, when the next generation of a country (craft) comes along with new ideas that no longer mesh with the alliance, when one of them keeps having problems and asking for help but will not accept outside advice. Etc. etc. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T11:54:45-08:00","id":1168871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1168862#post1168862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More like half a century, if you count its predeccesors. It means generations grown up without any wars within its borders and that we don't have to bother with paperwork within when traveling, etc. And I didn't say that that the EU will last, that's still up for grabs, neither did I suggested the same with the disparates. The thing is, it's an example that people could be willing to sit down and compromise, even after centuries upon centuries of grudges and after twice burning down the continent. It's possible. Yes, those old grievances and new interests might cause it to crumble, but seeing them making a starting attempt is not <i>that</i> stretching.</div> </div> </div> </div>But these groups, as written WON'T compromise. And the Book of Secrets rational for how to get groups of rabidly ethnocentric groups to function together are pretty much a recipe for disaster. These aren't grievances, they are core beliefs that don't allow for much bending before the group is going to break. Then you'll end up with, say, Taftani in the Disparates and other Taftani. Both of whom think of themselves as the REAL Taftani (and one of whom is more correct, and it's not the one in Alliance...)<br /> <br /> This isn't border crossing and work visas and cheeses, it's like Poland had slavery and Spain was all about the value of human freedom, that Italy thinks assassination is a legitimate way to handle political advancement while Denmark insists that all that matters is primogeniture in determining who should be leader (though those aren't opposites, man, will they EVER collide) or even just having France believing it is superior to all others and refusing to deal with the other nations unless they respected the innate superiority of the French. Then saying, &quot;Here are the Ten Commandments&quot; and having the Hague deal with all the conflicts by means of punitive justice with only one punishment available, execution.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1062,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","user":"Ajax","date":". 12-21-2017, 11:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T12:12:30-08:00","id":1168880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1168871#post1168871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But these groups, as written WON'T compromise.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the thing, that with all their incompatible beliefs and ethnocentrism and stuff, they're not just abstract groups, they're people in the setting. People could bend and give and there will be people, who will see the bigger picture and are willing to compromise. Of course there will be other people who will be hell-bent on the differences and condemn the compromists for treason and that's how you get extremist splinter groups.<br /> <br /> Or, as you suggested, the compromising party will be the minority and we'll see something like the sabbat, where the majority of the sect isn't from a &quot;native clan&quot;, but from antitribu.<br /> <br /> Another example is how a significant part of the Assamites approached the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> It's easy to say &quot;those won't work together, not for any reason, no way, it's anathema to the groups' ideologies. Know what? Given enough incentive, people will brush all of that under the carpet, even if for a short time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T17:19:17-08:00","id":1168956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1168815#post1168815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One sign to the contrary of that is that Technocracy characters were playable at the Berlin LARP, which has a significant place in the future metaplot. So, I don't think they'll go that far back to early Mage.<br /> <br /> As for Vampire, yes, I have too the definite impression that <i>at first</i> they want to go for an 1e feel. Although they said they <i>will</i> bring out the Sabbat, just not at the beginning, because they want to focus on the Cam vs. Anarchs thing at first. The Sabbat won't be an undefined boogeyman, they'll just show up later on.<br /> <br /> As I wrote earlier, I think it's most likely that extremist groups within both large organization will become more on the front and causing trouble, while the more moderate ones wanting to build bridges.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure there was a Vampire larp that had sabbat clans. I'm sure there will be &quot;Something&quot; with the sabbat I'm not sure it will be &quot;V:TM&quot; vs pulling off into a separate game. That being said the Sabbat isn't a major player in most of the world as of v5 which is pretty much where 1e started they were something that happened that was scary, but they weren't a major force vs the cam. The Cam feared mortals and anarchs and that's where we have v5.<br /> <br /> M5 is probably NOT going to have playable Technocracy to start. They will be very much pulled back, they might come back in a different game. but I don't think we are going to see them as anything but Antagonists for quite awhile. Especially since they DO seem to have taken up the role as cross gameline antagonists.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T17:54:01-08:00","id":1168960,"title":"","content":"I'm curious, why do you think it'll be separate games for those factions? As far as I know, there's a Sabbat book intended later on and they will have a major role in the metaplot. It just won't start with that, I think.<br /> <br /> Independents ditto.<br /> <br /> I think that yes, there is a clear message for going back to the 1e setup, with isolated cities, Cam vs. Anarchs, only the core 7 clans in the corebook and so on, but I don't think it'll stop there, given time and nothing they said indicated that for me so far. <br /> <br /> As for the Technocracy, remember, they weren't a playable faction with the corebook, really, in any edition, prior M20.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T18:02:05-08:00","id":1168962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1168880#post1168880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's the thing, that with all their incompatible beliefs and ethnocentrism and stuff, they're not just abstract groups, they're people in the setting. People could bend and give and there will be people, who will see the bigger picture and are willing to compromise. Of course there will be other people who will be hell-bent on the differences and condemn the compromists for treason and that's how you get extremist splinter groups.<br /> <br /> Or, as you suggested, the compromising party will be the minority and we'll see something like the sabbat, where the majority of the sect isn't from a &quot;native clan&quot;, but from antitribu.<br /> <br /> Another example is how a significant part of the Assamites approached the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> It's easy to say &quot;those won't work together, not for any reason, no way, it's anathema to the groups' ideologies. Know what? Given enough incentive, people will brush all of that under the carpet, even if for a short time.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sometimes. Yes. Just as often. No. Not at all. In fact, that &quot;maybe for a short time&quot; is probably the only way it would work And then usually only if there was some pressing concern, like, say, they had all been attacked by the Union, Traditions, or, even better for the current rhetoric, the Nephandi.<br /> <br /> But you look at these groups. They aren't &quot;people&quot; in the sense of being ordinary folks who happen to belong to some club. These groups are defined by their core beliefs and the fact that those beliefs are correct. It's small groups of insiders who don't really have the common ground you're presupposing. Not only don't they have a common enemy, they really don't have anything in common to drive this big sit down. No common borders. No issues of trade. No workers to exchange. Nothing. They are self-contained, self-involved and self-oriented.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T18:08:02-08:00","id":1168965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1168960#post1168960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious, why do you think it'll be separate games for those factions? As far as I know, there's a Sabbat book intended later on and they will have a major role in the metaplot. It just won't start with that, I think.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Technocracy has a major role in the Vampire metaplot that doesn't mean I don't think a more customized Technocracy game. Werewolves have a major role in the Vampire plot too. I think the Sabbat have different themes and moods that might cross into Camarilla stories but rather than having to work as a kludge that in someways undermines the idea of humanity Paths could function as theirown thing and setup.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think that yes, there is a clear message for going back to the 1e setup, with isolated cities, Cam vs. Anarchs, only the core 7 clans in the corebook and so on, but I don't think it'll stop there, given time and nothing they said indicated that for me so far.<br /> <br /> As for the Technocracy, remember, they weren't a playable faction with the corebook, really, in any edition, prior M20. </div> </div> </div>Given a push back towards 1e, I imagine Mage 5 will look more like Mage 1e than any other mage. More the fact that the Technocracy seems like it might be being used as a crossline antagonist may push it even farther from playablity and into full on &quot;antagonists only&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-21T07:33:43-08:00","id":1169346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1168880#post1168880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's easy to say &quot;those won't work together, not for any reason, no way, it's anathema to the groups' ideologies. Know what? Given enough incentive, people will brush all of that under the carpet, even if for a short time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like the Taftani brushed under the carpet their love for Vulgar magick to get economical power in Dubai?<br /> <br /> Yeah, that's exactly what we don't want to see, I think. Disparates were the mages that refused to compromise their core beliefs in order to work with others, even if that meant to die. That was the charm of these groups, their narrative-Mage it's basically saying &quot;enough with that, it's not fun to play with a fundamentalist&quot;<br /> <br /> Now, if the Aliance were formed by &quot;antitribu&quot;, there's a different problem: We already have a group where disparate societies of mystics can gather to practice their Paradigm with freedom as long as they agree to respect all other Paradigms-The Traditions. Disparates refused to join the Traditions because they didn't wanted to compromise-if they have changed their minds they have a potent group of mages right there that will receive them with open arms-Heck, in Revised this was the trend-&quot;moderate&quot; Children of Knowledge, Ngoma, Templars, Wu Lung, and others accepted to join the Traditions, these were the &quot;antitribu&quot;.<br /> Why not join them in good faith, then?. The reason given it's so preposterous as to form part of a Mind effect casted by a Nephandi or a Batini- &quot;we have no proff, but they may be corrupted. Unlike the other Disparate, who surely aren't corrupted even when we have no way to prove it&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 12-21-2017, 10:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-22T06:31:38-08:00","id":1169614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1168660#post1168660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Anarchs are just like that. As I said, I don't see the Disparates as a &quot;real&quot;, formal alliance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Anarchs still copy the power structure of Camarilla princes though; they lack a worldwide organization, but in every Anarch city we have a Baron with his own powerbase and right arms. Mages lack this kind of local gerarchic organization, unless they come from the same Tradition (and they usually don't).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I know that, but if I remember correctly, it was one person, but I might be wrong, I have to check. </div> </div> </div>No, a fair share of them followed the Horizon Warrior; and after the revolt was quelled they just brought Concordia down with them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1169346#post1169346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like the Taftani brushed under the carpet their love for Vulgar magick to get economical power in Dubai?<br /> <br /> Yeah, that's exactly what we don't want to see, I think. Disparates were the mages that refused to compromise their core beliefs in order to work with others, even if that meant to die. That was the charm of these groups, their narrative-Mage it's basically saying &quot;enough with that, it's not fun to play with a fundamentalist&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. I don't need more names for organized groups, I need flavour. The Taftani were a niche yet meaningful group, with enough significative differences from the other mages to actually make sense for them to stay apart; these modern Taftani could be easily absorbed by CoX or the Syndacate, or maybe live as orphans.<br /> <br /> Yes, I'm bitter about the Taftani rework. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-22T15:20:21-08:00","id":1169746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1169614#post1169614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, a fair share of them followed the Horizon Warrior; and after the revolt was quelled they just brought Concordia down with them.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, I asked it in the past several times and still, which book is in it? I'm not asking because I'm not believing you, I'd just like to read it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I have the Weinberg novel trilogy (albeit in Hungarian, is it's not entirely impossible that some things got cut out, for whatever reason) and I don't remember it.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-24T04:25:27-08:00","id":1170136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1169746#post1169746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, I asked it in the past several times and still, which book is in it? I'm not asking because I'm not believing you, I'd just like to read it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I have the Weinberg novel trilogy (albeit in Hungarian, is it's not entirely impossible that some things got cut out, for whatever reason) and I don't remember it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it was the namesake &quot;The Ascension Warrior&quot;, second in the trilogy. Or, as previously written, you can find a synopsis in &quot;Tales of Magick: Dark Adventures&quot; and some mention in &quot;Ascension&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-21T12:40:11-07:00","id":1261968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1168815#post1168815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One sign to the contrary of that is that Technocracy characters were playable at the Berlin LARP, which has a significant place in the future metaplot. So, I don't think they'll go that far back to early Mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? I have been worried about a reversion to 1e for the 'Crats if new-WW gets their hands on them and this seems to suggest otherwise.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As I wrote earlier, I think it's most likely that extremist groups within both large organization will become more on the front and causing trouble, while the more moderate ones wanting to build bridges. </div> </div> </div>That makes sense - a &quot;cold war&quot; feel for the Ascension War would definitely be different from the hot conflict it was in the 90s.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-21T16:00:42-07:00","id":1262012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1168727#post1168727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the Hollow Ones join the Disparate Alliance, anyone who would make war on them must suddenly make war on the Bata'a, the Templars, the Wu Lung, and those slippery Ahl-i-Batin.<br /> <br /> That's a fight even the Tradition mages would not relish. Especially since the Traditions already have their on-and-off conflicts with the Technocracy, who most would agree are the greater threat.</div> </div> </div> </div>This *would* be true...if the Disparate Alliance wasn't all hush-hush and a Big Secret (TM) that is being kept from the Traditions. Soooo...from the Tradition's point of view, the Hollow Ones are still running solo. And yes, it's kind of a conundrum. Act like you're running solo and risk being attacked, or reveal your big secret new club.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-22T01:20:11-07:00","id":1262084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1168379#post1168379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My best bet is that the traditions will get more fractured. The extremist groups will get more ground and they will be causing more problems internally and with the Union. At the same time I think the same will happen with the Union, as it strains under the conflict between the Orwellian (maybe Nephandi-influenced) part and the &quot;we genuinely want a better place for the masses to live in&quot; part. So I think the more moderate factions in both will close some distance between them and the extremist factions will be worse than ever and thus the strict Traditions vs. Technocracy dichotomy will loosen up.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that the writing in regard to the Technocracy shouldn't be as focused as it currently is on just these two groups or types of Technocrats - the ruthless and controlling Technocrats, and the idealists who want to be out there for mundane humans and to improve the mundane human societies. I do wish that this will change in future publications of M:tA ; and that other kinds and groups of Technocrats - who are already written about, just not as much as these two kinds of Technocrats that I wrote about above - will be described and outlined more. I think that M:tA would benefit from this as both a game and as a setting.<br /> <br /> What about the researchers and visionaries who just more or less don't care about ( for example ) mundane humans, or Tradition Mages ? In regard to other persons, they will act differently from situation to situation, and from person to person ; according to what occurs, and as per those of their particular personal values, biases, goals, and priorities will matter the most to them in a given situation ( While also taking the rules and guidelines of the Technocracy into account, to various extents ) .<br /> <br /> What about those Technocrats who simply are out there for themselves, their Amalgam, and their Convention ( in this, or a different order of priorities ) ? They do want to develop their knowledge and capabilities as a Technocrat Mage, and to acquire more influence, resources, and/or achievements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 10-22-2018, 04:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-22T07:34:26-07:00","id":1262135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1262084#post1262084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about the researchers and visionaries who just more or less don't care about ( for example ) mundane humans, or Tradition Mages ? In regard to other persons, they will act differently from situation to situation, and from person to person ; according to what occurs, and as per those of their particular personal values, biases, goals, and priorities will matter the most to them in a given situation ( While also taking the rules and guidelines of the Technocracy into account, to various extents ) .</div> </div> </div> </div>Since being in the Techno<b><i>cracy</i></b> it's a full time job that has everything to do with controling the world of humans and mages, as their name suggest, I would say that those would deserve a new terminology, similar to Roge but w/o the negative connotation. They're not Technocrats because they don't care about Control, but they do follow the rules set by the Technocracy and don't cause trouble. Sympathisers, perhaps?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-22T07:59:25-07:00","id":1262144,"title":"","content":"I've heard rumours as well that the Trads are going to be literal Reality Terrorists in M5 ... so imagine something similar to Revised with <i>both</i> the Traditions and the Technocracy being outright evil, for a worst-case scenario.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-22T10:16:18-07:00","id":1262178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1262135#post1262135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Since being in the Techno<b><i>cracy</i></b> it's a full time job that has everything to do with controling the world of humans and mages, as their name suggest, I would say that those would deserve a new terminology, similar to Roge but w/o the negative connotation. They're not Technocrats because they don't care about Control, but they do follow the rules set by the Technocracy and don't cause trouble. Sympathisers, perhaps?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't agree with the criterion you gave in regard to a Mage being a Technocrat. Descriptions of the Technocracy mention or imply that it is possible - with calling upon friends and contacts, having and calling upon personal achievements, knowledge, and power, and/or through skillful politics, and also through navigating the Technocracy's rules and duties - for a Technocrat to get away with ignoring or bending seemingly obligatory standards and rules within the Technocracy ; and that it happens regularly.<br /> I think a Mage is a Technocrat when the Mage uses technocratic methods and Foci - that were and are developed by the Technocracy - for what they do as a Mage and as a person ; while also being an active member of the Technocracy.<br /> Former Technocrats - who are no longer in the Technocracy, but still use technocratic Foci and methods successfully - could be considered and called technocratic Mages.<br /> <br /> Sympathizers is the term for mundane humans who are agents or retainers of Technocracy and who are partially initiated into the Technocracy's ideas and mission statement ; or depending how you look at it, presented a derivative version of these, one that is comprehensible for them. So another word for this kind of Technocrat Mages would be needed ; or the word ' sympathizer ' would have to be taken away from it's current use, to use it as a term for this kind of Technocrats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 10-22-2018, 01:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-22T16:28:58-07:00","id":1262251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Czernobog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1262144#post1262144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've heard rumours as well that the Trads are going to be literal Reality Terrorists in M5 ... so imagine something similar to Revised with <i>both</i> the Traditions and the Technocracy being outright evil, for a worst-case scenario.</div> </div> </div> </div>Worse, I wouldn't be too surprised, if they'd end up as genuine Reality Terrorists, <i>who are in the right</i>, from the standpoint of the game's narrative, because fuck Western civilization yadda-yadda.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I expect something similar to how they portrayed the Cam and the Anarchs in V5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 10-22-2018, 07:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-22T16:34:30-07:00","id":1262252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1262084#post1262084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that the writing in regard to the Technocracy shouldn't be as focused as it currently is on just these two groups or types of Technocrats - the ruthless and controlling Technocrats, and the idealists who want to be out there for mundane humans and to improve the mundane human societies. I do wish that this will change in future publications of M:tA ; and that other kinds and groups of Technocrats - who are already written about, just not as much as these two kinds of Technocrats that I wrote about above - will be described and outlined more. I think that M:tA would benefit from this as both a game and as a setting.<br /> <br /> What about the researchers and visionaries who just more or less don't care about ( for example ) mundane humans, or Tradition Mages ? In regard to other persons, they will act differently from situation to situation, and from person to person ; according to what occurs, and as per those of their particular personal values, biases, goals, and priorities will matter the most to them in a given situation ( While also taking the rules and guidelines of the Technocracy into account, to various extents ) .<br /> <br /> What about those Technocrats who simply are out there for themselves, their Amalgam, and their Convention ( in this, or a different order of priorities ) ? They do want to develop their knowledge and capabilities as a Technocrat Mage, and to acquire more influence, resources, and/or achievements.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not against more &quot;who care&quot; groups within the Union, but honestly, I wouldn't like the loosening up of the factions, especially the Union, after a point, because that'd take away a lot from the big philosophical and physical conflicts that make the game and setting interesting.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-22T16:34:37-07:00","id":1262253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1262251#post1262251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Worse, I wouldn't be too surprised, if they'd end up as genuine Reality Terrorists, <i>who are in the right</i>, from the standpoint of the game's narrative, because fuck Western civilization yadda-yadda.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I expect something similar to how they portrayed the Cam and the Anarchs in V5.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've also heard talk of them aligning the Traditions with <i>real</i> political and religious extremist groups. I shudder at the thought ...<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, isn't that likely to PO pretty much everybody who likes the Traditions, especially after M20 heavily pushed the idea that they were adapting to the modern world, and that this was a good thing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1410,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","user":"Czernobog","date":". 10-22-2018, 08:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-22T23:16:41-07:00","id":1262298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1262252#post1262252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not against more &quot;who care&quot; groups within the Union, but honestly, I wouldn't like the loosening up of the factions, especially the Union, after a point, because that'd take away a lot from the big philosophical and physical conflicts that make the game and setting interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that those two groups or attitudes that I mentioned are practically already present in write-ups of the Technocracy, even if they are not directly mentioned as distinct types of Technocrats. Nearly every write-up of Conventions mentions distinct and significant distance and divides between them ; who or what else could have caused this, but such Technocrats being members of the Technocracy ? I can see other reasons for the inter-Conventions situation(s) within the Technocracy being like this, but this reason seems to be one that is most tangible and direct ; and is also one that would lead to the inter-Convention relations and interactions staying like this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 10-23-2018, 02:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-23T07:58:37-07:00","id":1262359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Czernobog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1262253#post1262253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've also heard talk of them aligning the Traditions with <i>real</i> political and religious extremist groups. I shudder at the thought ...<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, isn't that likely to PO pretty much everybody who likes the Traditions, especially after M20 heavily pushed the idea that they were adapting to the modern world, and that this was a good thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>This would be very wrong, and it goes beyond &quot;adapting to the modern world&quot;. Traditions can be anty-science (though that would create a huge clash with the VA and Etherites), but they can't possibly be extremists:<br /> <br /> How it's an extremist christian so extremist if he's cooperating with a pagan witch to protect both Paradigms?. Extremist Christians posit that any other religion it's satanism undercover. Extremist christians also dislike atheists, but they would be much more at home among scientists and atheists than among actual demon summoners (OoH) or demon worshipers (Dreamspeakers, Verbena, Choristers that aren't Christian).<br /> <br /> Tradition has laws against not helping your fellows. There's NO WAY the Celestial Chorus can be composed of extremist people firts and foremost. Some could be extremists, and these would also be isolationists that only join in Chantries fully composed mages that follow the same religion and try to ignore all their less savory compatriouts except when they can use them as cannon fooder. An Extremist Chorister it's one step from going Roge all the time.<br /> <br /> Same goes, more or less, for the rest of the Traditions. <br /> <br /> Now, Orphans can be extremists, there's no problem with that because they don't have to side with people of different traditions. Non-allied Disparate can be extremists, Rogues can be extremists. All those who aren't actually figting back to back with people that has radically different Paradigms can be extremists: Traditions aren't among these.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 10-23-2018, 11:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-23T09:01:06-07:00","id":1262366,"title":"","content":"It is possible to make the Traditions extremists in the sense of willing to take extreme actions to bring about the ideals of the Traditions (paradigmatic freedom, free will, harmony, etc), but it would still be a bad move. Individual Traditionalists like Xoca make sense, as do Cabals of them, but the Traditions are supposed to work on multiple levels. Influencing the collective unconscious, verbal battles in academic publishing, racing for the resources of other worlds, running soup kitchens to affect people on a personal level, these are all valid moves in the Ascension War. Revised already made the mistake of trying to truncate that in favor of pushing players towards a specific style. Focusing on extremism seems to be the same mistake in a different direction.<br /> <br /> But I'm not going to worry about it too much until it becomes more than rumor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-23T09:02:53-07:00","id":1262367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Czernobog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1262253#post1262253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've also heard talk of them aligning the Traditions with <i>real</i> political and religious extremist groups. I shudder at the thought ...</div> </div> </div> </div>Won't be too surprised about that either. See what they did with the Brujah. I've said several times, but I'm expecting the Anarch book to end up more-or-less as &quot;Antifa: the Masquerade&quot;.<br /> <br /> The presentation in the mobile game wasn't too encouraging either.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> EDIT: Also, isn't that likely to PO pretty much everybody who likes the Traditions, especially after M20 heavily pushed the idea that they were adapting to the modern world, and that this was a good thing? </div> </div> </div>Even in Revised and earlier. Really, it was always like that, as I've seen it, that most mages aren't throwbacks. Old archamges, sure, but most of the Traditions' members, especially after the Avatar Storm were brought up in the modern world, with plumbing, electric lightning, cars, smartphones, in the case of the newer generations, internet, etc. They are not indoctrinated cultists of some religious extremist group out in the woods. There could be isolationist groups and chantires out there, but that's not the norm.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1683\" data-vbnamecard=\"1683\">Aleph</a> has wrote.<br /> <br /> But of course, that won't stop WW. If they want to make it Technocracy=evil capitalist white-Western patriarchy and Traditions=batshit-crazy religious fanatic terrorists and you supposed to play Orphans and Crafts (maybe the Disparate Alliance), beause of #street-level play and #personal stories, then, they'll do it. I wouldn't be too surprised about it, though I hope it won't end up like that, but V5 didn't make me to be too hopefull.<br /> <br /> Maybe the Disparates will start to take over, just like the Anarchs are taking over in V5 and the Traditions will mostly contain the real extremists, just like V5 Cam became the insular group of privileged high-class vampires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-25T06:51:53-07:00","id":1262672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1262367#post1262367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Won't be too surprised about that either. See what they did with the Brujah. I've said several times, but I'm expecting the Anarch book to end up more-or-less as &quot;Antifa: the Masquerade&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's hoping it doesn't.<br /> <br /> But I'm not hopeful, sadly.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-25T23:56:49-07:00","id":1262803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1262366#post1262366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> but the Traditions are supposed to work on multiple levels. Influencing the collective unconscious, verbal battles in academic publishing, racing for the resources of other worlds, running soup kitchens to affect people on a personal level, these are all valid moves in the Ascension War.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that somehow this behavior and approach, and the Mages who are doing this, would slowly but surely be the cause of - or at least contribute towards - some Mages of the Traditions becoming extremists and radicals. It is the combination of it being so mundane, it being about helping a relatively small number of mundane humans who can help themselves ( and if they can't, then someone else will give them the soup ) , and it being juxtaposed with ideals and goals of the Traditions faction and of individual Traditions, and also juxtaposed with the actions and plans of other Mages of the Traditions. I can see an Arete 1 or 2 Mage doing such charity work without causing much of a reaction and eyebrow raising ; but I think that after meeting for the fourth time a Mage with Arete 3 or more ( let alone a whole Cabal of them) who would be exemplifying this &quot; affect people on a personal level &quot; approach , some Tradition Mages would go radical and/or extremist as a reaction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 11-05-2018, 02:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-26T03:00:28-07:00","id":1262817,"title":"","content":"In short, I do think, given a couple of years that a M5 would be a good thing. Not to denigrate the work done with M20 (or M4 as it will be), and I will still be holding on to my dear Quintessential Edition, but I'd like to see some aspects of V5 enter into a re-development of the game ground up. Specifically:<br /> <br /> 1) A re-emphasis of 'Paradigm' over factions - that is, characters being based on their personal beliefs primarily, over and above any particular group affiliation. Politics can still be part of the game, but a character could study Hermetic magic without being part of an Order of Hermes, and so on. Following on, a lot of the various Traditions, Crafts and Conventions could be condensed down to a more manageable list (at least in the core-book). Something in the region of less than ten, inclusive of techno-magic types (so no need for the provision of additional Technocratic Union options). I'd actually reconsider the whole Technocratic War theme too, which may be a bit reminiscent of the Mage Revised era, but I honestly wonder whether its really a prominent theme in the current times. I think Nephandi could be more emphasised as the main big bad.<br /> <br /> 2) I really like the idea of having a mechanic similar to Hunger Dice, but based on Paradox.<br /> <br /> 3) Some of the concepts in the magic system could be tidied up a bit - Forces could be better defined, for example - where it's now loosely (and incorrectly) defined as 'elemental energies', it could be more correctly refer to the interactions and motions of physical things. A good review of the language and terminology of the game, generally, would be great.<br /> <br /> 4) A general review of the look and feel of the game, to match V5's 21st century look would certainly be interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","user":"Trippy","date":". 11-07-2018, 10:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-26T06:37:39-07:00","id":1262841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1262817#post1262817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) I really like the idea of having a mechanic similar to Hunger Dice, but based on Paradox.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wonder about that. Hunger Dice as it is is pretty much the worst type of wasted potential, where something possibly nice is instead akin to replacing your socks with sandpaper and running a marathon.<br /> <br /> Given Paradox is more about things going awry than losing control, I see the potential in that. But whoever writes it has to realize the mistake that hunger dice became.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-26T12:56:55-07:00","id":1262924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1262841#post1262841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder about that. Hunger Dice as it is is pretty much the worst type of wasted potential, where something possibly nice is instead akin to replacing your socks with sandpaper and running a marathon.<br /> <br /> Given Paradox is more about things going awry than losing control, I see the potential in that. But whoever writes it has to realize the mistake that hunger dice became.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having played V5 with my group, I don't think that Hunger Dice are a mistake at all. In fact, I can't really imagine playing Vampire in any satisfying way without them now. They evoke drama around the table, taking a narrative responsibility away from the ST in some ways, towards creating great stories. I think anybody who thinks they are a mistake hasn't actually used them in play.<br /> <br /> In the game we had this week for example, one Toreador character rolled a 'Messy critical' while questioning a crime witness. She interpreted the roll as being highly successful - the witness gave up all the information she was guarding - due to her using vampiric sexiness, and ended up giving her a Lingering Kiss. Now, during what was a routine scene, my Toreador player has now accumulated an obsessive fan, who she will be able to draw blood from on occasion, but will also have to manage the obsessiveness - it's become a really good plot device and player complication. The player loved this challenge, it brought out the themes of playing a Vampire character with personal style and it wouldn't have happened without the Hunger dice interacting at the table. In practice, we are finding that the Hunger dice seem to add about two extra, unscripted but very thematic scenes to every session we play. It's a brilliant mechanism.<br /> <br /> In Mage, this could also be a great way to really bring out some sort of Paradox interaction into play in a more spontaneous way. As with V5, there could be a section in the rules that highlighted different sorts of backlash that could be tailored to the situation or paradigm of the characters involved. And this, in my view, could work better than the current systems which rely on an element of ST fiat or player self management, and are consequently often forgotten about in play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","user":"Trippy","date":". 10-26-2018, 03:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-26T15:43:15-07:00","id":1262964,"title":"","content":"It may be of interest to note that Mage already uses dice to represent Paradox . The supreme difference here, I think, will be the way they're going to be used: As part of the roll rather than as a pool that appears only when there's a backlash.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippi</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And this, in my view, could work better than the current systems which rely on an element of ST fiat or player self management, and are consequently often forgotten about in play.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've never seen someone forget about their Paradox in play. It's such a huge deal in Mage - you're either gaining it or trying to avoid it all the time. I find rather hard to forget about it.<br /> <br /> Altrough I've seen people refusing to play Mage because in their opinion Paradox was too intrusive. I've never tought that myself, but my experience with other people it's that they overemphasise Paradox even beyond what the rules say on the matter. Who knows?, maybe the new edition will be fair to their expectations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-26T16:33:05-07:00","id":1262970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1262964#post1262964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It may be of interest to note that Mage already uses dice to represent Paradox . The supreme difference here, I think, will be the way they're going to be used: As part of the roll rather than as a pool that appears only when there's a backlash.<br /> <br /> I've never seen someone forget about their Paradox in play. It's such a huge deal in Mage - you're either gaining it or trying to avoid it all the time. I find rather hard to forget about it.<br /> <br /> Altrough I've seen people refusing to play Mage because in their opinion Paradox was too intrusive. I've never tought that myself, but my experience with other people it's that they overemphasise Paradox even beyond what the rules say on the matter. Who knows?, maybe the new edition will be fair to their expectations.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have, insofar, that Paradox is often treated as a bit of a chore for some STs and players, rather than an opportunity to really delve into some interesting scenarios. Some players just try to burn it off as a damage roll, rather than anything interesting. I've played in some groups that just try to avoid it altogether. Paradox shouldn't be a chore, and making an elegent mechanic to handle it and provoke a bit of story creation with it is a good thing. I do acknowledge that this is the intent with the current rules, but I think the mechanics of it could be improved in a manner similar to V5 (and Werewolf too with 'Rage' dice).<br /> <br /> A Hunger dice mechanic is pretty cool because it requires less book keeping (you would only have one track 1-5). Making a magical effect would generally have you rolling a Paradox check (6+ on a D10 roll for no consequence, and 1-5 accruing a Paradox point). Vulgar effects might have players roll more than one dice to check, so players would be encouraged to keep things low key and Coincidental. The accumulated Paradox points would be translated as Paradox Dice to be included in all dice pools, exchanging for a one for one basis (as with Hunger dice). If characters have a Paradoxical Failure (no successes rolled, and one or more Paradox dice showing '1's) or if they have a Paradoxical Critical (roll two '0's with one of them being a Paradox die), then they would incrue some sort of ironical backlash from the effect they cast previously.<br /> <br /> For example, say they cast an effect with Mind to make themselves invisible - accruing some Paradox along the way - and then get a backlash doing some other task later on - say driving in a car chase - then a Paradoxical Critical could be that your car seems to go invisible momentarily, bamboozeling your competitor who then crashes. A Paradoxical Failure, however, could have the character failing to perceive another vehicle in front of them and crashing. It's just a simple example, but it's really easy to interpret - because the situation has provided parameters for developing the narrative. Other informative aspects could include the paradigm of the character or just the STs narrative development of the story to suit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","user":"Trippy","date":". 11-07-2018, 10:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-26T18:20:45-07:00","id":1262977,"title":"","content":"The actual setup of &quot;special dice roll stuff = stuff happens&quot; is fine. It's why there's potential as a paradox mechanic.<br /> Hunger dice don't fail because of that. They fail because the compulsions are more ridiculous than not. It's loss of control done dumbly instead of interestingly.<br /> I'm happy for you that you find it interesting. I find it horrid.<br /> <br /> So, whatever form a hypothetical M5 paradox mechanic takes, I hope it's nowhere like the compulsions. Especially in a game like mage, where ceding to your inner demons is a &quot;wisdom&quot; issue rather than a &quot;you are a literal monster&quot; issue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-26T18:42:06-07:00","id":1262982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1262977#post1262977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The actual setup of &quot;special dice roll stuff = stuff happens&quot; is fine. It's why there's potential as a paradox mechanic.<br /> Hunger dice don't fail because of that. They fail because the compulsions are more ridiculous than not. It's loss of control done dumbly instead of interestingly.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not true. Firstly, all of the various compulsions discussed are open to interpretation by both the ST and player. Secondly, the ones discussed are varied and easy to tailor to different characters and situations. They aren't 'ridiculous' unless for some reason you go out of your way to make them so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, whatever form a hypothetical M5 paradox mechanic takes, I hope it's nowhere like the compulsions. Especially in a game like mage, where ceding to your inner demons is a &quot;wisdom&quot; issue rather than a &quot;you are a literal monster&quot; issue. </div> </div> </div>Obviously, the themes of Mage are different to Vampire, but the interactions of the Paradox can still be mechanically run in a similar way - just with different interpretations based on the Mage setting's themes.<br /> <br /> All the Hunger Dice, or Paradox Dice or whatever variation do is to take existing 'botch' and 'critical' mechanics and insert some specific themes, associated with the game, into them to create narrative opportunities. People seem to be reading way to much else into the idea, I feel. Mechanically speaking, it's no more of a 'loss of control' than what previously existed as 'botches' and 'critical successes'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","user":"Trippy","date":". 10-27-2018, 05:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-26T22:19:12-07:00","id":1263007,"title":"","content":"Dunno why you put botches and critical successes there. They don't compare to each other in that sense.<br /> Comparing &quot;failing to do something&quot; with &quot;you will now do something else&quot; makes little sense too.<br /> <br /> Anyway.<br /> You don't see a problem with the Compulsions as a concept. I do.<br /> Compulsions outright state that you will act discordantly with your intent. That you are given choices is less relevant than you make it sound to be. Something like this should occur from far more dramatic circumstances than just a lapse in restraint.<br /> If you want a constant risk to overlook your every roll it's simply better to work off an incentive/penalty system. Give the players bonuses to act out the hunger, penalties to suppress it and act normally. The narrative result is much the same, while giving a more enjoyable experience and demanding less fiat from the table when you really just want to work something in the scene and luck failed you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-27T01:03:05-07:00","id":1263029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1263007#post1263007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dunno why you put botches and critical successes there. They don't compare to each other in that sense.<br /> Comparing &quot;failing to do something&quot; with &quot;you will now do something else&quot; makes little sense too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mechanically, they absolutely do. The 'botch' was always about something happening that you didn't intend. The 'Critical' didn't technically exist in previous editions, but high degrees of success were always traded in for additional effects or happenings in the results of play.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Anyway.<br /> You don't see a problem with the Compulsions as a concept. I do.<br /> Compulsions outright state that you will act discordantly with your intent. That you are given choices is less relevant than you make it sound to be. Something like this should occur from far more dramatic circumstances than just a lapse in restraint.<br /> If you want a constant risk to overlook your every roll it's simply better to work off an incentive/penalty system. Give the players bonuses to act out the hunger, penalties to suppress it and act normally. The narrative result is much the same, while giving a more enjoyable experience and demanding less fiat from the table when you really just want to work something in the scene and luck failed you. </div> </div> </div>Where does the text of V5 actually say that? Where is the quote? I'll give you a hand by pointing out that it never says that. What is says is that a GM can either choose or randomly roll a Compulsion as appropriate to the situation, and the player can then choose how to act it out.<br /> <br /> And y'know, the whole point of the Beast in Vampire or Paradox in Mage, is that the characters <i>do not have</i> <i>control</i>. I mean that is what they both represent in their respective games.<br /> <br /> You can choose for yourself, what you find enjoyable as a system but frankly I find penalty/incentive systems so tedious and finickety to implement, in real game play, that players and STs tend to ignore them or just forget to use them. The dice rolls don't forget. As with all dice rolling mechanisms, dice rolls act to mediate the game in a non-arbitrary way and, in the case of mechanics like this, actually bring important themes of the game to the table. These themes frequently get overlooked by many players and groups in my experience (...of playing WoD games for over 25 years) - I've played in some groups that practically never do anything interesting with Paradox beyond burning out a few Health Levels now and then. If you don't like the risks of dice rolling, there is always diceless play to fall back on - which is a significant part of the V5 system as a whole and shouldn't be forgotten - but all dice rolling mechanics are unpredictable and add drama because of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","user":"Trippy","date":". 10-27-2018, 05:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-27T09:53:07-07:00","id":1263078,"title":"","content":"To each their own. If they try using a similar mechanic here at least I'm a little hopeful that something like the compulsions just won't make it. Quiet is a big deal rather than a standard ocurrence with paradox.<br /> But it doesn't matter, does it? Until it exists we're just speculating. We'll agree to disagree.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-27T11:34:40-07:00","id":1263104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1263078#post1263078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To each their own. If they try using a similar mechanic here at least I'm a little hopeful that something like the compulsions just won't make it. Quiet is a big deal rather than a standard ocurrence with paradox.<br /> But it doesn't matter, does it? Until it exists we're just speculating. We'll agree to disagree.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can be assured that even if they do go in this direction - which I hope they do - they won\u2019t be called \u2018Compulsions\u2019 as the theme of Mage is different. They\u2019ll be called \u2018Paradox Backlashes\u2019 which are already in the game. <br /> <br /> Either way, yes it is all speculation, so we can agree to disagree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-29T01:15:03-07:00","id":1263320,"title":"","content":"I think there is a way to put the Compulsions in M5 more or less as they are. It might be the Hubris and the Quiet, as they're both mess with mage's mind in similar manner to vampiric Compulsions.<br /> Btw, what's the source of these rumors about &quot;extremism&quot; in M5?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24623-dreamwalker","name":"Dreamwalker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-29T04:04:58-07:00","id":1263328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreamwalker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1263320#post1263320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Btw, what's the source of these rumors about &quot;extremism&quot; in M5?</div> </div> </div> </div>My guess?<br /> MAXIMUM EDITION ANGST way, way ahead of any actual work on-, or release of M5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-29T04:20:17-07:00","id":1263330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreamwalker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1263320#post1263320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Btw, what's the source of these rumors about &quot;extremism&quot; in M5?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pure speculation.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-31T15:34:45-07:00","id":1263906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreamwalker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1263320#post1263320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Btw, what's the source of these rumors about &quot;extremism&quot; in M5?</div> </div> </div> </div>I heard a rumour that M5 was being built on themes of &quot;terrorists vs. the surveillance state&quot; and jumped the gun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-03T14:34:40-07:00","id":1264498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Czernobog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1263906#post1263906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I heard a rumour that M5 was being built on themes of &quot;terrorists vs. the surveillance state&quot; and jumped the gun.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sounds terrible, but I expect little else after hearing about the directions of Vampire and Werewolf.<br /> <br /> Honestly I would like for any potential future editions to basically start the games over with some updates to better reflect the quarter century that's passed since they were first all dreamed up, and to be very light on the metaplot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","name":"Onkwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21481_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-03T14:48:53-07:00","id":1264499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Czernobog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1263906#post1263906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I heard a rumour that M5 was being built on themes of &quot;terrorists vs. the surveillance state&quot; and jumped the gun.</div> </div> </div> </div>...maybe they start on the premise that they are both wrong? That would be nice...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-03T15:23:05-07:00","id":1264503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Czernobog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1263906#post1263906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I heard a rumour that M5 was being built on themes of &quot;terrorists vs. the surveillance state&quot; and jumped the gun.</div> </div> </div> </div>To a degree, that's what the original game was - Traditions vs Technocracy. <br /> <br /> My view is that the work done to humanitise the Technocracy has made them a bit less placed as an uber-bad force in the game, while the current state of affairs in the 21st century leads me more in fear of losing a rational view of the world rather than being overwhelmed by it. <br /> <br /> If I was doing a new edition of the game, I would honestly consider smashing the whole emphasis on Traditions vs Technocracy - allowing mixed groups of PCs - and making the main villain the more insiduous drive of the Nephandi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-03T15:52:34-07:00","id":1264508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1264503#post1264503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I was doing a new edition of the game, I would honestly consider smashing the whole emphasis on Traditions vs Technocracy - allowing mixed groups of PCs - and making the main villain the more insiduous drive of the Nephandi.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't this the direction M20 is going in already?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-03T16:15:01-07:00","id":1264512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1264503#post1264503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> If I was doing a new edition of the game, I would honestly consider smashing the whole emphasis on Traditions vs Technocracy - allowing mixed groups of PCs - and making the main villain the more insiduous drive of the Nephandi.</div> </div> </div> </div>What is the difference between a Technocrat without Backing who can hang out with Tradition members and.. an Etherite or VA? I mean definately feel more like &quot;everyone lost the Nephandi are on top&quot; would be a solid place to start M5 but how do you have a Technocracy that.. is coherently different than Technoctrads without engagement?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-03T16:17:11-07:00","id":1264513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Czernobog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1264508#post1264508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Isn't this the direction M20 is going in already?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's true, and in terms of the humanising of the Technocracy, you could see it from one of the very earliest supplements for 1st edition - Book of Shadows anyway. Mage 1st edition really had the Technocracy as a boogeyman to regulate and threaten the characters - taking most of their cues from The Terminator and cold-blooded Men in Black. It was only in Book Of Shadows that they started to characterise them in a more human way - and it was also where they generally got into the depth of motivations behind certain other groups too.<br /> <br /> The problem now I think comes when there is too many factions and groups detailed. Currently, M20 has about 25 groups - 9 Traditions, 5 Conventions, and 10 or 11 Disparate groups, depending on whether you count Orphans. <br /> <br /> Now, some people love the diversity, so I'm not talking with a Word of God here, but I think it's quite a lot to get a handle on. I don't think there should be any distinction between Traditions and Disparate groups, and I could actually see alliances between Technocracy conventions and other groups too. By extension, I also think that some 'groups' are really just game contrivances rather than entitites that would actually be able to organise themselves in any global way. <br /> <br /> My thoughts for M5, amongst other things, is that there should be less group affiliations over all. I actually think you could remove the concept of the 'Traditions' altogether, essentially saying that all player Mages are Disparates, in effect.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-03T16:21:14-07:00","id":1264514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1264513#post1264513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that's true, and in terms of the humanising of the Technocracy, you could see it from one of the very earliest supplements for 1st edition - Book of Shadows anyway. Mage 1st edition really had the Technocracy as a boogeyman to regulate and threaten the characters - taking most of their cues from The Terminator and cold-blooded Men in Black. It was only in Book Of Shadows that they started to characterise them in a more human way - and it was also where they generally got into the depth of motivations behind certain other groups too.</div> </div> </div> </div>And now metaplot developments mean that we can have both inhuman pure-antagonist Technocrats and humanised PC-viable ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-03T16:29:41-07:00","id":1264516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Czernobog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1264514#post1264514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And now metaplot developments mean that we can have both inhuman pure-antagonist Technocrats and humanised PC-viable ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, to a degree, although the former type is of representation is kinda frowned upon now. <br /> <br /> The convention in the other classic WoD games is to have 13 factional groups - Clans, Tribes, or what-have-you. Do you think that the number of Mage groups could be condensed into that number also - whilst still managing to retain full options in play?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-03T16:34:06-07:00","id":1264520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1264516#post1264516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The convention in the other classic WoD games is to have 13 factional groups - Clans, Tribes, or what-have-you. Do you think that the number of Mage groups could be condensed into that number also - whilst still managing to retain full options in play?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would put the Traditions in the core and have the other two factions under &quot;Guide to the Technocracy&quot; and &quot;Guide to the Disparates&quot; supplements.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-03T16:47:08-07:00","id":1264523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1264513#post1264513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My thoughts for M5, amongst other things, is that there should be less group affiliations over all. I actually think you could remove the concept of the 'Traditions' altogether, essentially saying that all player Mages are Disparates, in effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Group affliliation allows crossing of concepts. Its my issue fundimentally with the DA. They don't believe eachother's magic should work.. while the Traditions accept on some level &quot;those guys don't quite get it.. but they have some ideas&quot;<br /> <br /> And I will ask again, what is a Technocrat who acknowledges Hermetic magic might have a purpose and can work with them.. that isn't a TechnoTrad? IF you loose affiliations why are there SOEs, VAs, IX, SYndicate etc?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-03T16:48:28-07:00","id":1264525,"title":"","content":"Never mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":21481,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","user":"Onkwe","date":". 11-06-2018, 09:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","name":"Onkwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21481_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-03T18:09:48-07:00","id":1264533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Czernobog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1263906#post1263906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I heard a rumour that M5 was being built on themes of &quot;terrorists vs. the surveillance state&quot; and jumped the gun.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't be too surprised if it would turn out like that. In fact, not at all and if so, there went my interst in it.<br /> <br /> Also, let's not get a chopper to the groups, affiliations and themes Mage has, just for the sake of making it easier to grasp, shall we? The complexity of those things, as well as yes, the big philosophical disagreements and antagonisms between the groups are what makes Mage interesting, in my eyes. Otherwise, I'd play Awakening.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-03T18:26:38-07:00","id":1264538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Czernobog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1264520#post1264520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would put the Traditions in the core and have the other two factions under &quot;Guide to the Technocracy&quot; and &quot;Guide to the Disparates&quot; supplements.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It's basically what they did with Mage revised, but it met with some hostility at the time. I'm going to give a speculative crack at how they could condense down the groups a bit - obviously YVMD, but it's just a few thoughts:<br /> <br /> I could see the <b>Progenitors</b> and <b>Void Engineers</b> moving away as Technocracy groups, and forming a new big collective Science! group along with the <b>Sons of Ether</b> and possibly even the <b>Virtual Adepts</b>. They'd need a new collective name, but maybe something like '<b>The New Order of Reason</b>' would work? - and would represent all the more 'experimental' scientific practitioners out there. Techno-magic, could be used by all groups of course, so there should be scope for plenty of character choice still.<br /> <br /> The <b>New World Order </b>could be condensed into <b>The Syndicate</b>, insofar that the Syndicate could be the upper echelons of the NWO, employing Men in Black, but more fundamentally driven by capitalism and economic control. <b>Iteration X </b>could be explanded as a group to incorporate the more hardline scientists that defect from the the old Progenitors and Void Engineers. So, fundamentally, <b>The Technocatic Union</b> (primarily as antagonists, but still playable in the same way the Sabbat are in Vampire), would be comprised of two groups: <b>The Syndicate </b>and <b>Iteration X.</b><br /> <br /> I'd keep all the various religious-orientated Traditions in tact: <b>Akashic Brotherhood</b> (or Record?), <b>Celestial Chorus</b>, <b>Euthanatos </b>(change the name to Chakravanti), reitroduce the <b>Ahl-i-Batin </b>to the 'Traditions' and also have <b>The Order of Hermes</b> as a 'broad church' group seeking to reassert magical and mystical paradigms of all sorts. The Solificati/Children of Knowledge would probably be reintegrated into a Hermetic House again, along with a <b>House Ngoma</b> (along with ten other Houses!). The <b>Verbena</b> might incorporate <b>Sisters of Hippolyta</b> (which actually, I think is a cooler name), and the Knights Templar could be a wing of the <b>Celestial Chorus</b>. I'd disband the notion of collective '<b>Dreamspeaker'</b> and '<b>Cult of Ecstacy</b>' groups, and instead just refer to a plethora of independent 'Disparate' shaman/ecstatic groups. Simlarly, the <b>Hollow Ones</b> would be part of a collective group just refered to as Orphans. 'Paradigms' would be chosen independently from group affiliation anyway, and so players could still play these kinds of characters, just without being shot-horned into a contrived group.<br /> <br /> So\u2026a M5 'Tradition' list could be:<ul><li><b>The Ahl-i-Batin</b> - fully reintegrated into a formal Tradition (again).</li> <li><b>The Akashic Record</b> - Largely as before, with a more inclusive name. More emphasis on the actual records, and connections to internet..</li> <li><b>The Celestial Chorus</b> - Incorporating Knights Templar and generally Christian or monotheic groups</li> <li><b>The Chakravarti</b> - As with the old Euthanatos, but more influenced by Sanskrit based traditions. Reincarnation and life/death cycle beliefs.</li> <li><b>The Disparates</b> - incorporating any shamanic or ecstatic (or any other) Mage from any culture. Represents lots and lots of dicverse and disparate groups.</li> <li><b>The New Order of Reason</b> - Incorporating Sons of Ether, Virtual Adepts, Progenitors, Void Engineers or any other 'free thinking' science-based 'magic'.</li> <li><b>The Order of Hermes</b> - 12 Houses, incorporating House Ngoma and House Solificati and obviously having a diversity of other types of 'Western Occult' mages.</li> <li><b>The Orphans</b> - being any Mage rejecting societal grouping; independents. Again, represents all sorts of individual mages.</li> <li><b>The Verbena </b>- incorporating Sisters of Hippolyta, and possibly also a few Ecstatic mages.</li> </ul>Standing slightly apart, mainly as antagonists:<ul><li><b>The Syndicate</b> - Incorporating the New World Order as an agenda, and largely interested in dominating economics, politics and social sciences.</li> <li><b>Iteration X</b> - Incorporating aspects of the Progenitors and Void Engineers, and largely interested in creating a single mechanistic paradigm.</li> <li><b>The Nephandi</b> - Possibly alien entities looking to corrupt and destroy human beliefs aspiration - an Anti-Ascension group - who may or may not have infiltrated the other two groups and possibly a number of other groups too. And <u>this</u> would be the fundamental conflict in the game.</li> <li><b>The Marauders - </b>Less of an organised group and more of a phenomenon, that can potentially afflict any Mage.</li> </ul>Which adds up to a 'mystical' 13 groups, which could all be called &quot;Traditions&quot; if we'd like, and would be the equivalent to Vampires 13 Clans and Werewolves 13 Tribes. Oh, and I would refrain from trying to officially match up each group to a particular Sphere (let players come up with their own interpretations, and choose their own specialities). Characters would be able to choose their Paradigm as a separate thing, so you could have a Hermetic Mage that studies Voudun, a New Order of Reason Mage researching spiritualism (or 'parapsychology'), a Gnostic based Celestial Chorus practicising ecstatic magic, a Kung-Fu fighting Orphan, or any other sort of combination of beliefs.<br /> <br /> How'd ya do all this? Well, have a metaplot suggest that the Ascension War intensified in the 21st century leading to a break up of lots of the existing groups and a fundamental re-organising of others into a new political situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","user":"Trippy","date":". 11-03-2018, 09:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-05T10:36:16-08:00","id":1264754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1262803#post1262803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that somehow this behavior and approach, and the Mages who are doing this, would slowly but surely be the cause of - or at least contribute towards - some Mages of the Traditions becoming extremists and radicals. It is the combination of it being so mundane, it being about helping a relatively small number of mundane humans who can help themselves ( and if they can't, then someone else will give them the soup ) , and it being juxtaposed with ideals and goals of the Traditions faction and of individual Traditions, and also juxtaposed with the actions and plans of other Mages of the Traditions. I can see an Arete 1 or 2 Mage doing such charity work without causing much of a reaction and eyebrow raising ; but I think that after meeting for the fourth time a Mage with Arete 3 or ( let alone a whole Cabal of them) who would be exemplifying this &quot; affect people on a personal level &quot; approach , some Tradition Mages would go radical and/or extremist as a reaction.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Some definitely. The aforementioned Xoca is a good example. My only issue is if that becomes the dominant attitude of the Traditions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-05T22:26:38-08:00","id":1264883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1264513#post1264513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that's true, and in terms of the humanising of the Technocracy, you could see it from one of the very earliest supplements for 1st edition - Book of Shadows anyway. Mage 1st edition really had the Technocracy as a boogeyman to regulate and threaten the characters - taking most of their cues from The Terminator and cold-blooded Men in Black. It was only in Book Of Shadows that they started to characterise them in a more human way - and it was also where they generally got into the depth of motivations behind certain other groups too.</div> </div> </div> </div>1e also had the first Technocracy books, which were ... not that good, and not really coherent at all, really. Stuff like NWO Agents summoning Paradox spirits to sic on their foes (at only Spirit 2, no less!), mixed with Devices that were blatantly magic items without even a thin hypertech veneer, nonsensical and counter-productive Evil Technocratic Plots (which in certain cases were extremely offensive out-of-universe) and a whole load of random nonsense. Some of that stuff was so bad it was quietly retconned and never mentioned again.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-06T08:26:42-08:00","id":1264974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1264754#post1264754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Some definitely. The aforementioned Xoca is a good example. My only issue is if that becomes the dominant attitude of the Traditions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if you ask me it could happen. For example assuming that there would be a lot of those Mages in the Traditions, that I referred to in my previous post, who focus primarily on interacting with and helping mundane humans. And assuming that there would be a reaction or a backlash of sorts in the Traditions against this kind of attitude and approach, that would result in many Mages of Traditions becoming radicals and/or extremists in their outlook and actions.<br /> <br /> Or it could happen because of many Tradition Mages focusing on developing the theory and the practice of Magick to the exclusion of other goals and aspirations.<br /> It could also happen because of individual Traditions - or factions within individual Traditions - seeking to define themselves as definitely distinct and separate from other groups within the Traditions.<br /> <br /> Though I think that this should not be the main direction or circumstance under which to develop and define the Traditions as a faction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 11-06-2018, 11:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-06T08:40:33-08:00","id":1264983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1264974#post1264974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, if you ask me it could happen. For example assuming that there would be a lot of those Mages in the Traditions, that I referred to in my previous post, who focus primarily on interacting with and helping mundane humans. And assuming that there would be a reaction or a backlash of sorts in the Traditions against this kind of attitude and approach, that would result in many Mages of Traditions becoming radicals and/or extremists in their outlook and actions.<br /> <br /> Or it could happen because of many Tradition Mages focusing on developing the theory and the practice of Magick to the exclusion of other goals and aspirations.<br /> It could also happen because of individual Traditions - or factions within individual Traditions - seeking to define themselves as definitely distinct and separate from other groups within the Traditions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it's possible, simply because the Dark Ages recidivists and paradigmatic extremists of the Traditions went off to their own Horizon realms ... and were destroyed by the Avatar Storm. The vast majority of traditionalists alive today in the modern setting were born and raised amongst modern tech.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-06T20:11:38-08:00","id":1265201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Czernobog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1264883#post1264883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1e also had the first Technocracy books, which were ... not that good, and not really coherent at all, really. Stuff like NWO Agents summoning Paradox spirits to sic on their foes (at only Spirit 2, no less!), mixed with Devices that were blatantly magic items without even a thin hypertech veneer, nonsensical and counter-productive Evil Technocratic Plots (which in certain cases were extremely offensive out-of-universe) and a whole load of random nonsense. Some of that stuff was so bad it was quietly retconned and never mentioned again.</div> </div> </div> </div>A number of 1st Edition books were pretty awful. The first set of Convention books didn't suggest that the groups include playable types at all, of course. <br /> <br /> For me, Mage has always been something of a flawed masterpeice - sublime to ridiculous and all in between. M20 tries to consolidate everything into a whole - and having a single developer/writer does aid in this. It's just that the end result is a bit ginormous, and I feel could be reduced to a more practical game and setting only with a bit of radical pruning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-07T01:17:43-08:00","id":1265223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1264538#post1264538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could see the <b>Progenitors</b> and <b>Void Engineers</b> moving away as Technocracy groups, and forming a new big collective Science! group along with the <b>Sons of Ether</b> and possibly even the <b>Virtual Adepts</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the goal and aspiration for these two Conventions would be primarily developing the theory and practice of science and Enlightened Science, then why would they leave the Technocracy ? The Technocracy provides them with stability, opportunities to gain and share knowledge, and logistics. Also, to put it simply - the Technocracy is wholly ( or almost wholly ) focused on science in regard to their methods and interests ; while if these two Conventions would join the Traditions, they would belong to a faction that is inclined towards and focused on mysticism, which I think could be problematic for them due to various reasons.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1264538#post1264538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]<b>The Nephandi</b> - Possibly alien entities looking to corrupt and destroy human beliefs aspiration - an Anti-Ascension group - who may or may not have infiltrated the other two groups and possibly a number of other groups too.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does surprise me how often corruption and destruction get mentioned in regard to the Nephandi ; rather than gaining power, advancing in Magick capabilities and knowledge, or acquiring influence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1264538#post1264538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd disband the notion of collective '<b>Dreamspeaker'</b> and '<b>Cult of Ecstasy</b>' groups, and instead just refer to a plethora of independent 'Disparate' shaman/ecstatic groups.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that Traditions and M:tA as a setting would not be the same without the Cult of Ecstasy Tradition. First, the combination of their Paradigm and outlook, the ecstatic methods and practices, and the focus on Time Magick, is very characteristic and unique ; in M:tA it notably stems, to an extent, from the Cult's history. Not only are the Cultists of Ecstasy focused on Time Magick ; they are also distinguished by being more extreme - in their outlook and in their actions - and more distinctly defined than other ecstatic Mages. Their practices and pleasures are at the same time the goal, the aspiration, and the method to reach them, in a way that is clearly refined due to their values, perspectives, and approaches as an organization.<br /> The Cult of Ecstasy - partly because of their focus on Time Magick, which in M:tA is more than divinations - has no real-world group that they can be compared to. This makes them excellent in emphasizing and underlining the qualities and themes of M:tA.<br /> <br /> Also, how would the Cult of Ecstasy stop being a separate Tradition, assuming it would happen as an in-setting event ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-07T02:32:50-08:00","id":1265233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1265223#post1265223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If the goal and aspiration for these two Conventions would be primarily developing the theory and practice of science and Enlightened Science, then why would they leave the Technocracy ? The Technocracy provides them with stability, opportunities to gain and share knowledge, and logistics. Also, to put it simply - the Technocracy is wholly ( or almost wholly ) focused on science in regard to their methods and interests ; while if these two Conventions would join the Traditions, they would belong to a faction that is inclined towards and focused on mysticism, which I think could be problematic for them due to various reasons.</div> </div> </div> </div>They would leave it, as a metaplot device, if they felt that goals and objectives they roriginally joined up for had become corrupt. <br /> <br /> In my conception of the metaplot development, I would have the Technocracy being weakened - essentially splitting it - and theis may or may not be because of Nephandi infiltration. The 'purists' who support Enlghtened Science would leave because they might uncover darker developments that eschew their values - and as such push them towards finding alternative memberships.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It does surprise me how often corruption and destruction get mentioned in regard to the Nephandi ; rather than gaining power, advancing in Magick capabilities and knowledge, or acquiring influence. </div> </div> </div>Are these two things mutually exclusive? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think that Traditions and M:tA as a setting would not be the same without the Cult of Ecstasy Tradition. First, the combination of their Paradigm and outlook, the ecstatic methods and practices, and the focus on Time Magick, is very characteristic and unique ; in M:tA it notably stems, to an extent, from the Cult's history. Not only are the Cultists of Ecstasy focused on Time Magick ; they are also distinguished by being more extreme - in their outlook and in their actions - and more distinctly defined than other ecstatic Mages. Their practices and pleasures are at the same time the goal, the aspiration, and the method to reach them, in a way that is clearly refined due to their values, perspectives, and approaches as an organization.<br /> The Cult of Ecstasy - partly because of their focus on Time Magick, which in M:tA is more than divinations - has no real-world group that they can be compared to. This makes them excellent in emphasizing and underlining the qualities and themes of M:tA.<br /> <br /> Also, how would the Cult of Ecstasy stop being a separate Tradition, assuming it would happen as an in-setting event ? </div> </div> </div>There is a real world equivement to ecstatic style magic. The notion of using drugs and other sensory experiences to drive magic(k) is actually a fairly staple practice in the occult. In a sense, Aleister Crowley practiced ecstatic magic, but he did so still within a Hermetic understanding of it. While I agree that the Cult of Ecstasy is a colourful group, the actual paradigm and practice could be seperated from the need for a group to affiliate with. Indeed, any Mage could use it - either from a mystical Tradition (like the Order of Hermes, Ahl-i Batin or a gnostic-driven Celestial Chorus mage) or from a more modern perspective (in which case, I'd probably just make the same type of mage as a Dispirate or Orphan).<br /> <br /> Either way, what I am trying to get at is not every single practice or paradigm automatically needs to be catered for by a contrived group association. Indeed, having less group affiliations actually provides more options for Mages to be individualised. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-07T03:04:23-08:00","id":1265235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1265233#post1265233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are these two things mutually exclusive?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that ' destruction ' as a faction's goal is to a significant extent exclusive, and disruptive, to other goals, values, or aspirations that a faction might have.<br /> As far as I remember, I never see acquiring power, Magickal knowledge, or influence get mentioned on this forum as goals of the Nephandi. It is always corruption or suffering.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1265233#post1265233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a real world equivement to ecstatic style magic. The notion of using drugs and other sensory experiences to drive magic(k) is actually a fairly staple practice in the occult. (...)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes it is ; but those practices don't have the terms that the Cult of Ecstasy has, and the associated outlook and approaches : Kamamarga, Lakashim, Code of Ananda ( And the issues and questions associated with the Code Ananda ; the fact that the Code exists is directly due to many Cultists of Ecstasy - and before, the Seers of Chronos - having a tendency to act and think in ways that are counter to it. ) . The Cultists of Ecstasy also have this attitude and view point of &quot; If only more persons could enjoy life and tried to find ecstasy in what they do and who they are... &quot; that I think is very characteristic and distinct.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 11-07-2018, 06:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-07T06:11:04-08:00","id":1265258,"title":"","content":"I agree that Extatics would loose a lot if they became a practice. More so, <i>the Traditions would loose a lot</i>: There needs to be a faction focused on the passion and the irrational - in a sense they're the most direct enemies the Technocratical Paradigm has within the Traditions: The ones claiming absolute freedom from the world shakes, the anty-vulcans, <i>the ones claiming pure reason and logic it's fundamentally wrong</i>. They're the spirit of the Traditions (hence it's very appropriate that Sh'zar was the one that founded the Traditions in the first place). They're the ones who balance the OoH more nuanced take on mysticism. <hr /><br /> In fact, I would propose to make the Akashics a faction of the Extatics, and use the Extatics as the core to build the new Traditions:<br /> <br /> Extatics would be the faction who catters to irrational and passional magick all arround the world. Be it about the extremes of human experience or the void of meditation. Rather than having a Paradigm or a etnicity (like the Akashics have) they would be a more overaching group where every deeply irrational, paradoxical, passional, Paradigm it's welcomed.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile the OoH I would redefine as the group that catters ritual mages all around the world. Again, it wouldn't be so much an ethnicity or Paradigm as a certain approach to magick: A more rational and nuanced approach than the Cult, but deeply mystical nevertheless. Parts of every Tradition could end here.<br /> <br /> And those 2 would be the heart of the Traditions, the &quot;declaration of intent&quot; if you want, although not the only members.<br /> <br /> The Chakravanti already are decoupled from Paradigm, being about Deat and the police/judges of the Traditions.<br /> <br /> The core of the Dreamspeakers and A LOT of others could be reworked as the Shadow Talkers: a group focused on the Umbra that is all about interacting and getting power from otherwordly entities (for instance, an ufologist could easily end here if he keeps close encounters with EDE).<br /> <br /> A New Order of Reason could take the torch of Reason (Etherites/VA) as Trippy proposes, but I wouldn't make the VE join them.<br /> <br /> I would reverse the roles Trippy proposed for the Technocracy and make the Syndicate fold into the NWO. Because while money and the system are important, the Technocracy don't work as interesting antagonists for unafiliated mages without the concept of Control. I would also keep the Void Engineers as part of the Technocracy because the protection of earth deserves a group. That would make the Techncoracy a group of 3.<br /> <br /> Batini, Choristers, Verbena could form a faction that centers arround the concept of Faith, which it's also an important element of Mage (belief it's power, but it can be rational or irrational).<br /> <br /> That with Rogue, Disparate, Marauders and Nephandi makes 13 &quot;Clans&quot; (although personally I don't see much need to keep with Vampire numerology)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 11-07-2018, 09:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-07T06:20:06-08:00","id":1265263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1265235#post1265235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that ' destruction ' as a faction's goal is to a significant extent exclusive, and disruptive, to other goals, values, or aspirations that a faction might have.<br /> As far as I remember, I never see acquiring power, Magickal knowledge, or influence get mentioned on this forum as goals of the Nephandi. It is always corruption or suffering.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you need power to destroy, influence to corrupt...that your end goals aren't about power, knowledge or influence doesn't mean that these aren't aspirations (even values) too.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-07T09:21:03-08:00","id":1265293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1265263#post1265263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, you need power to destroy, influence to corrupt...that your end goals aren't about power, knowledge or influence doesn't mean that these aren't aspirations (even values) too.</div> </div> </div> </div>From how the Nephandi are presented and defined, it clearly seems to me it is power, knowledge, material wealth, and influence that are general ( or common ) end goals for them. Corruption - as in, convincing other persons that the Nephandi's radical methods and outlooks have more merit and advantages than seems at first - also is important, but to a lesser extent. Corruption could also be called propaganda ; though it is propaganda with a rather dark bent to it.<br /> <br /> While it is relatively often mentioned in M:tA books that the Nephandi have plans or intentions of bringing Earth to ruin ( sometimes with the aid or in agreement with beings from outside the earthly reality ) , this is contradicted, directly and indirectly, in many places. I consider the parts that might seem like talking about the Nephandi as wanting only to destroy and cause suffering to be ( too ) dramatic and expressive way of writing and choice of words ; or to be written from perspective of Mages hostile and/or ignorant in regard to the Nephandi.<br /> <br /> The overall idea that I get about the Nephandi is that they are the setting's most skilled and accomplished black ( or dark ) Mages ; or at least this is what the Nephandi want to achieve. And in addition to this, the Nephandi are the principal occult group that managed to delve into knowledge and mysteries in regard to the infernal, the Wyrm, and the lovecraftian. What each Nephandus, and each Nephandi group, wants to do and does with the power and the knowledge that they have is up to each Nephandus to decide.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-07T10:13:59-08:00","id":1265307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">While it is relatively often mentioned in M:tA books that the Nephandi have plans or intentions of bringing Earth to ruin ( sometimes with the aid or in agreement with beings from outside the earthly reality ) , this is contradicted, directly and indirectly, in many places.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've never seen those contradictions, I would love to see a few of those many direct contradictions you mention, because it's easy to make up indirect stuff.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, I bet you won't find any place in all of Mage history where the ultimate goals of the Nephandi <i>as a faction </i>are stated that doesn't include some mention of bringing ruinin to Earth. Prove me wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-07T10:50:57-08:00","id":1265316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1265258#post1265258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That with Rogue, Disparate, Marauders and Nephandi makes 13 &quot;Clans&quot; (although personally I don't see much need to keep with Vampire numerology)</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see a need for this either - in fact fundamentally in the current set-up there are only three main factions, each with a lean towards part of the Metaphysical Trinity, and two factions of Fallen Mages, to which I would add a third:<br /> <br /> <b>The Disembodied</b><br /> <br /> The ultimate warning against Paradigmatic extremism, the Disembodied are beings created when a Mage stays in the Umbra too long. They were relatively small in number until the events of 1999, when the Avatar Storm stranded thousands of Mages of both main factions which existed at the time behind the Gauntlet and away from Earthly Quintessence. As they became Spirits, they were forever locked in a state of <i>stasis</i>, unable to learn or grow. Now they exist as manifestations of their respective Paradigms, taken to inhuman and often horrific extremes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1410,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","user":"Czernobog","date":". 11-07-2018, 01:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-07T10:53:40-08:00","id":1265317,"title":"","content":"I am pretty excited for the prospect of M5. I think my biggest fear is that they will dumb down the idea of consensual reality and the flexibility of the Spheres. These are always the hardest things for new players to wrap their head around, but for me they are what make Ascension my all-time favourite game. I think there is definitely potential to use a Hunger-esque system for Paradox, and I really liked the suggestions that Trippy made a few pages ago.<br /> <br /> As for the fluff, I don't mind some changes. The Union has been on the brink of civil war for a while now, so it wouldn't surprise me if they didn't exist in the same configuration moving forward. Reading this thread, I see some people bristle at the notion of treating the Traditions in a more negative light. Your game is your game, but I always treated both sides as being morally complex, neither good or bad. The primary theme of Mage, from a player perspective (and of course, in my opinion), is hubris, and that should affect every faction.<br /> <br /> Nor am I overly concerned about injecting politics into the game, because they have always been there to begin with. Mage has always been about the battle of ideas, and if it needs to update itself a little bit to feel relevant to today, I see no issue with that. And honestly, the furor over the politics of V5 (amusingly accused of fascism by some, and social justice politics by others) is overblown to my reading. I don't really think there is anything to be concerned with. M20 is pretty much my perfect rendition of Mage, and I don't really see the value in a new edition that doesn't do things at least a little differently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24186-emmameta","user":"emmameta","date":". 11-07-2018, 01:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24186-emmameta","name":"emmameta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-07T11:09:47-08:00","id":1265322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>emmameta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1265317#post1265317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Your game is your game, but I always treated both sides as being morally complex, neither good or bad. The primary theme of Mage, from a player perspective (and of course, in my opinion), is hubris, and that should affect every faction.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes.The central conflict in Ascension is between the two main sides' incompatible visions of Mass Ascension - unlike in Awakening where it's between the faction that wants Mass Ascension to happen and the one that wants to stop it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-07T11:22:56-08:00","id":1265324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Czernobog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1265322#post1265322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes.The central conflict in Ascension is between the two main sides' incompatible visions of Mass Ascension - unlike in Awakening where it's between the faction that wants Mass Ascension to happen and the one that wants to stop it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Y'see the thing was, back in the 1990s, that the Technocracy reflected real world fears about a big 'One True Wayism' dominating world affairs which made the post-modernist Traditions seem really relevent in Mage. These days, however, I really don't see a big fear abroad about the drive of scientific beliefs eradicating cultures in the same way. If anything, I see scientific rationality under pressure. If we can imagine the themes of the game shifting from Mage: A Sorcerer's Crusade, then I think the situation for Mage has changed again in the 21st Century. I see the rise of the Nephandi, over and above the power of the Technocracy these days.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-07T11:47:49-08:00","id":1265336,"title":"","content":"There are many ways to make the Traditions very dark, even fanatical, in ways that none of the arguments of this thread would apply<br /> <br /> For instance, Traditions could easily be reality terrorists killing people for enlightenment. One of the themes of the game it's the debate betwen Freedom and Security. As the faction that catters freedom it would be appropiate if the Trads don't care too much for security. If the world Acends as a consequence, who cares if a few hundreds of millons die in the process?<br /> <br /> However, they can't possibly tolerate real life religious fanatics or fundamentalists, because these would be more prone to kill the other Traditions than to fight the Technocracy. The Traditions don't work without tolerance <i>because they have to tolerate each other</i>. That was the whole of my argument against that idea. To make them anty-science would fly on the face of Etherites/VA, but would be more likely than making them religious fanatics.<br /> <br /> There are lots of ways to make the Traditions dark and edgy, even fanatical, w/o straining belief. Turning them into anty-science religious fanatics isn't one of them. The Traditions have their own brand of fanaticism, represented in dudes like Xoca, that isn't really compatible with real life fundamentalisms. If Xoca was a religious fanatic, killing those who oppose his belief, then the other Traditions who follow a different religion would have as much or more to fear from him than Technocrats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-09T14:16:49-08:00","id":1265921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1265324#post1265324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Y'see the thing was, back in the 1990s, that the Technocracy reflected real world fears about a big 'One True Wayism' dominating world affairs which made the post-modernist Traditions seem really relevent in Mage. These days, however, I really don't see a big fear abroad about the drive of scientific beliefs eradicating cultures in the same way. If anything, I see scientific rationality under pressure. If we can imagine the themes of the game shifting from Mage: A Sorcerer's Crusade, then I think the situation for Mage has changed again in the 21st Century. I see the rise of the Nephandi, over and above the power of the Technocracy these days.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Which is why I think M20 made a good decision to have the default antagonists be the Nephandi, who are rising in power specifically because the two main sects were two busy focused on each other to notice them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-09T14:59:49-08:00","id":1265937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Czernobog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1265921#post1265921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Which is why I think M20 made a good decision to have the default antagonists be the Nephandi, who are rising in power specifically because the two main sects were two busy focused on each other to notice them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, although what I'm basically arguing is to go a step further and condense the Traditions, Crafts and some of the Technocracy Conventions into a smaller number of broader groups. It streamlines the game a lot in practical terms, but also gives developers a chance to review the backstory of the game towards updating it's 21st Century relevance.<br /> <br /> As we've both suggested now, the Technocracy are really not the \u00fcber-baddies they originally were in 1st edition. The Nephandi, however, are foremost now as a threat. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-10T16:12:32-08:00","id":1266285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1265937#post1265937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree, although what I'm basically arguing is to go a step further and condense the Traditions, Crafts and some of the Technocracy Conventions into a smaller number of broader groups. It streamlines the game a lot in practical terms, but also gives developers a chance to review the backstory of the game towards updating it's 21st Century relevance.<br /> <br /> As we've both suggested now, the Technocracy are really not the \u00fcber-baddies they originally were in 1st edition. The Nephandi, however, are foremost now as a threat.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I have to say that I think your &quot;New Order of Reason&quot; as a concept is somewhat flawed - if I was to split the Technocracy it would be Void Engineers + reformists/idealists in all four other Conventions + Virtual Adepts. The SoE would stay with the Traditions, for Paradigmatic reasons and their beef with the Void Engineers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1410,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","user":"Czernobog","date":". 11-10-2018, 08:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-10T16:39:07-08:00","id":1266290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Czernobog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1266285#post1266285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have to say that I think your &quot;New Order of Reason&quot; as a concept is somewhat flawed - if I was to split the Technocracy it would be Void Engineers + reformists/idealists in all four other Conventions + Virtual Adepts. The SoO would stay with the Traditions, for Paradigmatic reasons and their beef with the Void Engineers.</div> </div> </div> </div>The fundamental objective I am trying for is to find common ground with <i>playable </i>groups, as opposed to antagonist groups. Certain groups are more sympathetic than others.<br /> <br /> In the case of the backstory I am thinking of, I'd have it that the old Technocratic Union is increasingly corrupted (by Nephandi, primarily), to the extent that all right minded Scientific Mages within it would be repulsed enough to seek to break away tand form a new group - based on the founding principles of the original Order of Reason (from medieval times). In fact, I'd find that many of the more anarchic Virtual Adepts and Sons of Ether would possibly end up more as Disparates, although some would join up again with this 'New Order of Reason'. Once formed, it might seek to develop relationships with what they consider misguided, but less malevolant Traditions - like the Order of Hermes. Other Traditions may have also been corrupted, altered or destroyed by Nephandi infiltration too - leading to lots of Disparates and Orphans and with some groups returning from 'exile' or whathaveyou (basically using the metaplot to reconstruct as much as I like!).<br /> <br /> The main change, overall, would be a restructuring of the Traditions to be more inclusive of 21st century paradigms - including Scientific ones - in the face of a more apparent and unifying threat of The Nephandi and corrupted Technocracy essentially destroying all hope of any form of positive Ascension. I'd actually relish having a playable group of largely incompatable paradigmantic beliefs. Having a rationalist mage interacting with religious, mystical and spiritual mages would be great roleplaying fodder for me, and reinforces some of the themes that have always been present since the original game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","user":"Trippy","date":". 11-10-2018, 07:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-11T13:23:10-08:00","id":1266484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1265258#post1265258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree that Extatics would loose a lot if they became a practice. More so, <i>the Traditions would loose a lot</i>: There needs to be a faction focused on the passion and the irrational - in a sense they're the most direct enemies the Technocratical Paradigm has within the Traditions: The ones claiming absolute freedom from the world shakes, the anty-vulcans, <i>the ones claiming pure reason and logic it's fundamentally wrong</i>. They're the spirit of the Traditions (hence it's very appropriate that Sh'zar was the one that founded the Traditions in the first place). They're the ones who balance the OoH more nuanced take on mysticism.<br /> <br /> (...)<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Another quality I like in the Cult of Ecstasy is them having one very wide, but definitely distinct criterion for who can be a member - following an activity ( or an idea ) with passion that elevates a person to new heights ; with a characteristic focus given to feeling pleasure and ecstasy.<br /> <br /> I also like the idea - though I don't think it is stated anywhere directly - that the Cult's outlook, methods, and approaches can guide and turn any passion or activity that a Cultist of Ecstasy chooses to be their Kamamarga into an affinity and skill in Time Magick. A new member likes working out a lot ? She'll easily get Internal Clock and time divinations out of it. Another new member's passion is reading whole books without a break ? He'll easily get Internal Clock and time divinations, as well, because of this. I think this emphasizes very well the specialness and marvel that being a Mage in WoD can be.<br /> I prefer this to be true - that this affinity for Time Magick is a specialty of the Cult's of Ecstasy ; rather than that skill with and understanding of Time Magick comes easily to any Mage who has ecstatic activities as a Focus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 11-30-2018, 01:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-30T10:14:05-08:00","id":1272011,"title":"","content":"A few thoughts:<br /> <br /> 1 I think there are quite a few people out there, myself included, that liked elements of both ascension and awakening and would not mind M5 taking the best of both worlds. Especially i think some of the mechanics were better and clearer in awakening and while i love the basic set up of the acsension war i much prefer the more localized and modular aspects that M20 seemed to take from awakening. <br /> <br /> 2 On mechanics I would particularly like to see the spheres work a bit more like the arcana in so far as they don;t require so much combination with other spheres to produce common effects<br /> 3 I would also like to see a reworking of paradox. Love the idea but never liked any of the systems! . <br /> <br /> 4 I i liked the way that M20 was pointing to an greater focus on nephandi as a significant faction in the ascension war, both in terms of having been a corrupting force in the technocracy and as a separate force. The former point allows for more division within the technocracy and more opportunity to take the unity out of the Union and allow for more factions either breaking away from the Technocracy or fighting to save it from itself. This provides for more nuanced and varied kinds of interactions with the traditions. I also like the idea that Traditions and Technocracy might start realizing that, like the warring families in Game of Thrones, they have been fighting among themselves over who gets to rule reality while ignoring the far more dangerous threats to reality posed by the nephandi and marauders, and that this might again reorient the game to be about a different and more complex ascension war that involves more alliances with people you don't like but need to deal with bigger and more pressing problems. This has been a direction they have been moving since revised and and definitely in M20 but I'd like to see that explored further. <br /> <br /> 5 With respect to the V5 controversy and its impact on M5 and W5, i would suggest a greater realization &quot;in game&quot; that despite their pretensions otherwise, supernaturals are rarely in the drivers seat on real world events. they may nudge and influence and they may definitely take advantage of awful things being perpetrated by human actors but they are not the driving forces. That seems more real to me and i have never been a big fan of conspiracies, and even less so now considering the real world damage that conspiracy thinking is doing in real world politics. This way avoids the major pitfall (that V5 fell into) of attributing real world and difficult issues to supernatural interference in a way that is problematic for many.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12792-scifirabbi","name":"scifirabbi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12792_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-30T15:39:15-08:00","id":1272055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1265307#post1265307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've never seen those contradictions, I would love to see a few of those many direct contradictions you mention, because it's easy to make up indirect stuff.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, I bet you won't find any place in all of Mage history where the ultimate goals of the Nephandi <i>as a faction </i>are stated that doesn't include some mention of bringing ruinin to Earth. Prove me wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here are quotes - some the direct contradictions that I mentioned - from the second &quot; Book of Madness &quot; :<br /> <br /> &quot;The motivations, approaches and tactics of Nephandi can be as varied as you want them to be.&quot;<br /> States that the Nephandi can have other motivations than destruction or corruption.<br /> <br /> &quot;Of all the Nephandic sects, it is the infernalists who cling most tightly to the illusion that they have some control over their situation.&quot;<br /> &quot;Other have more hopeful notions. Some claim that their masters will allow them to live on, to rule the surviving human population in a time of smoke and desolation. This train of thought is particularly favored among Infernalist Nephandi, who eagerly await the day that they can serve their Princes' will on earth as governors of Hell's newest province.&quot;<br /> <br /> This contradicts these sentences that say that Nephandi, due to being Nephandi, wish to destroy the world and only want suffering. One whole sub-faction of the Nephandi is stated to have an entirely other goal. If the Nephandi are unavoidably predisposed towards wanting to destroy, how is it that the Infernal Nephandi have somehow adopted another outlook ? I have no way to reconcile these contradictory texts other than to consider that the authors used much too strong words when talking about the Nephandi in the sentences that say that the Nephandi only want to destroy and cause suffering ; I don't think those sentences are meant to be taken literally.<br /> Also I think that &quot; who cling most tightly &quot; in this quoted sentence might be an implication that there are other Nephandi than Infernal Nephandi who have this outlook.<br /> <br /> &quot;Often villains are fond of claiming that they are misquoted, or misunderstood, or really oppressed heroes whose names have been unjustly tarred by vengeful enemies. Not so the Nephandi. They know what they are and they accept it, with no mamby-pamby moralizing or angst-ridden bemoaning of the fact.&quot;<br /> This precludes the Infernal Nephandi from somehow being unaware of what and why they want ; thus establishing that it is possible for Nephandi to have non-destructive outlook and approach.<br /> <br /> In regard to the Nephandi and how to consider them, I think that it is a question:<br /> Are the Nephandi meant to be a faction of refined black Mages which, to a large extent, has been presented in M:tA books ( due to mistakes made in writing ) as a group solely focused on destruction, corruption, and suffering as goals to the exclusion of other possible aims and motivations ?<br /> Or are the Nephandi meant to be such a group with such narrow goals, that turned out to be much more interesting, intriguing, and complex ; and grew beyond the initial narrow concept ?<br /> I think that it is the first option. It has to be noted that the Nephandi are one of the three principal Mage faction in M:tA , next to the Traditions and the Technocracy. With &quot; Book of the Fallen &quot; due to be written, they will have their own book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 11-30-2018, 06:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-30T16:27:44-08:00","id":1272073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1272055#post1272055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> In regard to the Nephandi and how to consider them, I think that it is a question:<br /> Are the Nephandi meant to be a faction of refined black Mages which, to a large extent, has been presented in M:tA books ( due to mistakes made in writing ) as a group solely focused on destruction, corruption, and suffering as goals to the exclusion of other possible aims and motivations ?<br /> Or are the Nephandi meant to be such a group with such narrow goals, that turned out to be much more interesting, intriguing, and complex ; and grew beyond the initial narrow concept ?<br /> I think that it is the first option. It has to be noted that the Nephandi are one of the three principal Mage faction in M:tA , next to the Traditions and the Technocracy. With &quot; Book of the Fallen &quot; due to be written, they will have their own book.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually think its the second option. It seems to me that Nephandi and marauders started as secondary villains, focussing on destroying or unraveling reality while the traditions and technocracy focussed on creating it in their respective images. From a conceptual point of view I think the difference between nephandi and marauders originally was why they wanted reality destroyed and maybe how -Nephandi for their dark masters to rebuild it in THEIR images and marauders just cos! But as time went on (and maybe as more people like me started using cthulhu scenarios for their Mage games!) Nephandi became more complex and grew beyond their initial concept into a more fully formed faction. But In some ways the literature still hasn't fully caught up (although maybe it will in M20) and I would like to see it do so in M5. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12792-scifirabbi","name":"scifirabbi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12792_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-01T07:05:27-08:00","id":1272170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>scifirabbi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1272073#post1272073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(...) But as time went on (and maybe as more people like me started using cthulhu scenarios for their Mage games!) Nephandi became more complex and grew beyond their initial concept into a more fully formed faction. But In some ways the literature still hasn't fully caught up (although maybe it will in M20) and I would like to see it do so in M5.</div> </div> </div> </div>The M20 Corebook outright states, in a separate paragraph entirely about it, that the Nephandi don't serve the Nephandi Patrons / Infernal Princes / beings from the Deep Umbra / Dark Lords ; these beings are a source of considerations and inspiration for the Nephandi.<br /> <br /> Your mention of specifally &quot;cthulhu scenarios&quot; does surprise me a bit. The K'llashaa, the lovecraftian Nephandi, barely got developed compared to the Infernal Nephandi ( The Malfean Nephandi also have very, very little written in regard to them - but in their case information from W:tA can be used. ) . This is especially visible when one is aware the amount and variety of literature by H.P Lovecraft ( and other writers ) that can be used as material pertinent to developing the K'llashaa as distinct group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-01T14:14:25-08:00","id":1272235,"title":"","content":"Above all else, I want an up-to-date, refined system of magick that gives new-level mages a chance to pull off cool shit without being unduly penalized, and is clear and simple enough to adjudicate throughout play. I'd also like a focus on Orphans, with both the Technocracy and Traditions (and even the Disparates) seeming like relics from an obsolete Cold War of Magick, with the Nephandi and Marauders being looming threats that the Orphans end up dealing with because of the aforementioned Cold-War paralysis. Help me as a player make a consistent enough paradigm, let my magick do cool things, and let me struggle on my own or not from my character's point of view. The rest, let me use it as ideas to embrace or rebel against.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-02T09:32:57-08:00","id":1272401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1272170#post1272170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The M20 Corebook outright states, in a separate paragraph entirely about it, that the Nephandi don't serve the Nephandi Patrons / Infernal Princes / beings from the Deep Umbra / Dark Lords ; these beings are a source of considerations and inspiration for the Nephandi.<br /> <br /> Your mention of specifally &quot;cthulhu scenarios&quot; does surprise me a bit. The K'llashaa, the lovecraftian Nephandi, barely got developed compared to the Infernal Nephandi ( The Malfean Nephandi also have very, very little written in regard to them - but in their case information from W:tA can be used. ) . This is especially visible when one is aware the amount and variety of literature by H.P Lovecraft ( and other writers ) that can be used as material pertinent to developing the K'llashaa as distinct group.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So first, in my game I always focused more on the infernalists, who as i understood it did, in some way at least, serve these patrons. It is also, i believe stated that nephandi, encourage cults and i run with that! <br /> <br /> As for the distnction between the loveraftian nephandi and the malfean, I will admit to playing a bit fast and loose with that in so far as liberally interpreting the chthulhu scenarios to fit a more WoD cosmos and not being just literally about just teh mythos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12792-scifirabbi","name":"scifirabbi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12792_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-03T08:19:54-08:00","id":1272625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>scifirabbi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1272401#post1272401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So first, in my game I always focused more on the infernalists, who as i understood it did, in some way at least, serve these patrons. (...)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that if this happens, then the Infernal Nephandi serve in the sense of being a person that could be compared to, for example, a majordomo serving a ruler. For the Nephandus the relation is not disadvantageous or detrimental.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 12-03-2018, 11:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-04T08:31:46-08:00","id":1272849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1272055#post1272055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Here are quotes - some the direct contradictions that I mentioned - from the second &quot; Book of Madness &quot; :</div> </div> </div> </div>1\u00ba. When you provide quotes - especially cherry picked one liners - it's a good idea to include page number. Otherwise it's necessary to scan the whole book to find your particular line in it's context and that can be a thankless task.<br /> <br /> Other than that, let's remember contradictions <i>to what</i> I asked for:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>While it is relatively often mentioned in M:tA books that the Nephandi have plans or intentions of bringing Earth to ruin ( sometimes with the aid or in agreement with beings from outside the earthly reality ) , this is contradicted, directly and indirectly, in many places.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>So, you need quotes to<i> contradict that the Nephandi (plural) have plans or intentions of bringing Earth to ruin</i>.<br /> <br /> Yes?<br /> <br /> Well...<br /> <br /> Let's begin from the most egregious example:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;Of all the Nephandic sects, it is the infernalists who cling most tightly to the illusion that they have some control over their situation.&quot;<br /> &quot;Other have more hopeful notions. Some claim that their masters will allow them to live on,<b> to rule the surviving human population <u>in a time of smoke and desolation</u></b>. This train of thought is particularly favored among Infernalist Nephandi, who eagerly await the day that they can serve their Princes' will on earth as governors of Hell's newest province.&quot; </div> </div> </div>How it's &quot;A time of <i>smoke and DESOLATION</i>&quot; not equivalent to &quot;bringing Earth to ruin&quot;?<br /> <br /> You know what DESOLATION means when isn't used to describe an emotion?<br /> <br /> THIS:<br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">1.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">a state of emptiness or destruction.</span></span><br /> <br /> Which doesn't need to mean Absolute Void, but can also mean things like a not nice Wasteland or the Hell on Earth that your quote makes reference to. In general it's rather compatible with the meaning of RUIN. All of which makes me think you aren't employing the regular, most accepted, meaning of the words you're using. Why?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This contradicts these sentences that say that Nephandi, due to being Nephandi, wish to destroy the world and only want suffering. One whole sub-faction of the Nephandi is stated to have an entirely other goal. If the Nephandi are unavoidably predisposed towards wanting to destroy, how is it that the Infernal Nephandi have somehow adopted another outlook ? I have no way to reconcile these contradictory texts other than to consider that the authors used much too strong words when talking about the Nephandi in the sentences that say that the Nephandi only want to destroy and cause suffering ; I don't think those sentences are meant to be taken literally. </div> </div> </div>SO. If my evil master promises me I'm going to be spared after having &quot;a time of smoke and desolation&quot; befall on Earth and give me power over the desolate remains of humanity then I'm totally not having destructive goals that would ruin Earth. That's your logic?. If they don't want to kill everyone - even themselves - then they aren't trying to bring <i>ruin to Earth</i>?. The expresion &quot;ruling over the ruins&quot; doesn't ring a bell?<br /> <br /> Some Nephandi believe (and the obvious meaning of the first phrase: &quot;clinging to an illusion&quot; it's that they believe wrongly) they will have good lives<i> after ruining Earth</i> (a time of smoke and desolation) for everyone that's not them...<br /> <br /> How it's all of that &quot;ruling over the ashes&quot; talk a contradiction to the goal of <i>bringing Earth to ruin</i>?. How it's that bringing this &quot;time of smoke and desolation&quot; isn't a destructive goal?.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also I think that &quot; who cling most tightly &quot; in this quoted sentence might be an implication that there are other Nephandi than Infernal Nephandi who have this outlook. </div> </div> </div>Having went over the unavoidable and crushing fact that this outlook it's also all about ruining Earth, your quote only directly implies that this rather apocaliptic outlook it's the most optimistic one. That it's, it implies that<i> every other Nephandic outlook</i> it's even more apocaliptic that ruling over the smoking ruins of Earth.<br /> <br /> So, now that the quote that affirms egregiously that Nephandi do want to bring Earth to ruin (sometimes with the illusion of being allowed to rule over the ruins) has been analized, we can go to the one that isn't so destructive for your point but it's useless devoid of context:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;The motivations, approaches and tactics of Nephandi can be as varied as you want them to be.&quot;<br /> States that the Nephandi can have other motivations than destruction or corruption. </div> </div> </div>No, it states that Nephandi have varied motivations, approaches and tactics. Motivations to do what?, Approaches to what?, Tactics to achieve what?. Devoid of context that phrase means nothing. In English that can mean a lot of things depending on the context.<br /> <br /> For instance, if the context of these &quot;motivations&quot; was &quot;motivations to be a Nephandi&quot;, then it doesn't contradict that their goals are bringing ruin, because these goals could be assumed whitin &quot;being a Nephandi&quot;<br /> <br /> I could say that the motivations the Nephandi has (to bring ruin to Earth) can be as varied as you want (maybe you hate the world, maybe you want to stop suffering, etc.). In the same vein they could employ varied approaches and tactics to bring ruin.<br /> <br /> Now, if you hadn't cherripicked that line devoid of context, it may actually have said something that would bring water to your theory. I don't know because you've not provided a page number and thus I can't find it whitin it's context (and even then the goals of some aren't the goals of the faction, but since you haven't provided anything to think that a given Nephandus might have less than destructive goals I don't see a need to diferentiate here).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;Often villains are fond of claiming that they are misquoted, or misunderstood, or really oppressed heroes whose names have been unjustly tarred by vengeful enemies. Not so the Nephandi. They know what they are and they accept it, with no mamby-pamby moralizing or angst-ridden bemoaning of the fact.&quot;<br /> This precludes the Infernal Nephandi from somehow being unaware of what and why they want ; thus establishing that it is possible for Nephandi to have non-destructive outlook and approach. </div> </div> </div>Only if you prove that they aren't all about bringing Earth to ruin. If you haven't then the fact that Nephandi, as villans, are aware of what they do only proves that it isn't possible for them to have a trully non-destructive goal even if they ALSO seek domination (but never devoid of ruin, not even in the most optimistic cases it seems)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 12-04-2018, 12:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-05T08:35:21-08:00","id":1272972,"title":"","content":"My understanding is that the Nephandi are by definition destructive and corrupt and seek to bring the earth to ruin. What varies is what they think the world will look like after that destruction and what their role will be. For some, probably the ones who are actually right about what will be left, they are just nihilists, fully expect the earth to be utterly destroyed and they just want to be there to see the world burn with them included. Others think they will be the rulers of the (better to rule in Hell that to serve in heaven). And others believe they are engaging in creative destruction, destroying teh world so it can be remade in the image of their dark patrons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12792-scifirabbi","name":"scifirabbi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12792_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-05T09:36:10-08:00","id":1272981,"title":"","content":"The Nephandi grew more complex and more relevant to the setting over the years but they are never going to be a fully formed and coherent faction. Partly that is because they do not have a shared Paradigm, ideology, or mythos, only a specific metaphysical quality and a vague, general goal. Partly it is because they are supposed to be a cipher that other Mages cannot understand. It would limit a lot of their utility if we ever got a simple, understandable explanation of what they actually believe.<br /> <br /> All Nephandi are ultimately destructive, their inverted Avatars have seen to that. How they are trying to be, why they are trying to be, and if they are trying to be can all vary, but that doesn't change that original fact. Even those who say they want to serve in Hell will continue to be corrupt, corrosive, and destructive if Hell is all that is left.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-06T05:54:35-08:00","id":1273081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1272981#post1272981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All Nephandi are ultimately destructive, their inverted Avatars have seen to that. How they are trying to be, why they are trying to be, and if they are trying to be can all vary, but that doesn't change that original fact. Even those who say they want to serve in Hell will continue to be corrupt, corrosive, and destructive if Hell is all that is left.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, while all Nephandi are destructive, and certainly they want to bring doom to the world, I think that the idea that they will be corrosive e<i>ven for the standards of Hell</i> it's a call of a higher order. As far as I know Nephandi were always depicted as pure evil and destruction lovers, but were never declared to be more destructive or somehow worse than the demons they sumon.<br /> <br /> However, I think M20 may be following that idea, insofar as Nephandi are described as <i>using </i>their &quot;patrons&quot;rather than worshipping them. I think that M20 may push the idea that &quot;Hell on Earth&quot; it's just a step closer to their final goal.<br /> <br /> Perhaps Nephandi that want to &quot;rule in hell&quot; are akin to the normal mages that can't Ascend because they are lost to the &quot;illusion of power&quot;, while more enligthened Nephandi seek the Truth in the Absolute Void of Nonexistence (which does mirror the idea of &quot;overcoming the need of power&quot; that Ascencion supposedly represents). But then again in Ascencion Al-Aswad was very comfy rulling in Hell...I think we don't have enough data on Nephandi to know for sure.<br /> <br /> That's why I think that having more data on Nephandi could be useful. Even if humans can't understand them, the ST should know how to use them: How a Nephandi &quot;progresses&quot; trough their various Ranks? How Descencion, Anty-Seekings, and Arete manifests for them? What kind of deals do they make with the forces of the Outer Dark, since they would refuse to worship them as per M20?.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 12-06-2018, 09:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-06T06:10:30-08:00","id":1273083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1273081#post1273081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, while all Nephandi are destructive, and certainly they want to bring doom to the world, I think that the idea that they will be corrosive e<i>ven for the standards of Hell</i> it's a call of a higher order. As far as I know Nephandi were always depicted as pure evil and destruction lovers, but were never declared to be more destructive or somehow worse than the demons they sumon.<br /> <br /> However, I think M20 may be following that idea, insofar as Nephandi are described as <i>using </i>their &quot;patrons&quot;rather than worshipping them. I think that M20 may push the idea that &quot;Hell on Earth&quot; it's just a step closer to their final goal. But I think we need to get more data on Nephandi before knowing for sure.<br /> <br /> That's why I think that having more data on Nephandi could be useful. Even if humans can't understand them, the ST should know how to use them: How a Nephandi &quot;progresses&quot; trough their various Ranks? How Descencion, Anty-Seekings, and Arete manifests for them? What kind of deals do they make with the forces of the Outer Dark, since they would refuse to worship them as per M20?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's not so much a matter of what the Nephandus wants, though, it's what their Avatar does. The Fallen Mage may think she has the world exactly the way she wants but her Avatar isn't going to stop pushing its destructive impulses just because she's content. Contentedness is not something Avatars are usually interested in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-06T06:29:48-08:00","id":1273087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1273083#post1273083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not so much a matter of what the Nephandus wants, though, it's what their Avatar does. The Fallen Mage may think she has the world exactly the way she wants but her Avatar isn't going to stop pushing its destructive impulses just because she's content. Contentedness is not something Avatars are usually interested in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. That's why I added, a bit too late:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>I</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps Nephandi that want to &quot;rule in hell&quot; are akin to the normal mages that can't Ascend because they are lost to the &quot;illusion of power&quot;, while more enligthened Nephandi seek the Truth in the Absolute Void of Nonexistence (which does mirror the idea of &quot;overcoming the need of power&quot; that Ascencion supposedly represents). But then again in Ascencion Al-Aswad was very comfy rulling in Hell...I think we don't have enough data on Nephandi to know for sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>We really need to know more about their Avatars than we do. Is Descencion to achieve the Void?. Maybe it is. But is Descencion so easy to reach?, perhaps even with Inverted Avatars being so pushy some Nephandi will never reach that level of &quot;anti-enlightenment&quot; (they don't seem to increase their Arete much faster than normal mages, as far as I know. Do they?).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-06T09:26:46-08:00","id":1273109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1166925-mage-5-and-a-new-vision?p=1273081#post1273081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps Nephandi that want to &quot;rule in hell&quot; are akin to the normal mages that can't Ascend because they are lost to the &quot;illusion of power&quot;, while more enligthened Nephandi seek the Truth in the Absolute Void of Nonexistence (which does mirror the idea of &quot;overcoming the need of power&quot; that Ascencion supposedly represents). But then again in Ascencion Al-Aswad was very comfy rulling in Hell...I think we don't have enough data on Nephandi to know for sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, I admit, that's a really good analogy. The only response I have to that is that there's some indication that Inverted Avatars can be more demanding or influential than regular ones. Mainly the way Widderslainte children act even before their awakening. Since we don't fully know if the Avatar is part of the soul or not (and for the record, I don't want that question answered) it is hard to say how meaningful that is.<br /> <br /> I agree we could use a bit more information. Not enough to make the Nephandi coherent, but perhaps enough to know how their Avatar affects their behavior. I would say in regards to your question &quot;Is Descension to achieve the Void?&quot; that it's not even clear regular Avatars know what Ascension is. They might know more about it than their Mages do, or at least have a slightly better idea of its direction, but that's about all we can say. So I think it's highly likely that inverted Avatars don't know if Descension is the Void. They still pull that way, or at least they pull towards incomprehensible things that lay in the same apparent direction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}